1
00:02:53,041 --> 00:02:55,458
2010
NAGPUR, MAHARASHTRA

2
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,916
[railway announcement]

3
00:02:58,916 --> 00:03:00,583
Tea? Snacks?

4
00:03:02,041 --> 00:03:03,416
Tea? Tea?

5
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,875
Tea? Tea?

6
00:03:05,125 --> 00:03:06,458
Piping-hot tea?

7
00:03:06,541 --> 00:03:07,791
Tea? Tea?

8
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:10,208
Tea? Tea?

9
00:03:10,916 --> 00:03:12,333
Want some tea?

10
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:13,583
Want some tea?

11
00:03:13,583 --> 00:03:15,333
Give me that bag. I'll keep it here.

12
00:03:15,625 --> 00:03:17,083
Brother... I want to sit here.

13
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:18,125
No. Go sit there.

14
00:03:18,166 --> 00:03:19,541
I want to sit here only.

15
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:22,166
This is my seat. You go sit there.

16
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:23,125
Umma...

17
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:24,416
Hey, kids! You want biscuits?

18
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:26,083
You want biscuits?

19
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:27,250
Ten rupees.

20
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,375
[train horn blaring]

21
00:03:30,125 --> 00:03:32,416
[train screeching to a halt]

22
00:03:32,458 --> 00:03:33,833
I want to sit here.

23
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,458
You go sit there.

24
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,291
Ticket?

25
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:48,708
Ticket?

26
00:03:51,333 --> 00:03:52,666
You have it, right?

27
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,500
-His ticket?
-He's not five yet.

28
00:04:02,666 --> 00:04:04,500
He looks older than five.

29
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,708
No. He isn't five yet.

30
00:04:05,750 --> 00:04:07,708
No, no. He is definitely older than five.

31
00:04:07,708 --> 00:04:09,041
No, he isn't.

32
00:04:22,833 --> 00:04:24,083
Pathu...

33
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,583
Umma... Pathu!

34
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:28,416
Pathu... Where's our daughter?

35
00:04:28,666 --> 00:04:29,708
Sweetie!

36
00:04:29,791 --> 00:04:31,125
Pathu!

37
00:04:31,791 --> 00:04:32,833
Pathu!

38
00:04:32,875 --> 00:04:35,000
Did you see my daughter?

39
00:04:36,375 --> 00:04:37,958
Did you see my daughter?

40
00:04:38,916 --> 00:04:40,125
Pathu?

41
00:04:40,916 --> 00:04:42,125
My child...

42
00:04:42,375 --> 00:04:44,166
Pathu!

43
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:49,458
[music swells]

44
00:05:07,291 --> 00:05:11,916
PART ONE
AJEEB RAHMAN - OFFICER ON PROBATION

45
00:05:11,916 --> 00:05:13,875
[train passing]

46
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,500
[suspenseful music playing]

47
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:34,666
[phone ringing]

48
00:05:37,541 --> 00:05:40,208
Don't forget to bring the notes
you dictated last week.

49
00:05:40,333 --> 00:05:42,500
<i>-I won't!</i>
-I need to finish them today.

50
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,791
<i>Yeah, I'll bring them.</i>

51
00:05:45,041 --> 00:05:46,791
Listen... Policeman is up.

52
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,500
<i>-Hang up then.</i>
-Alright.

53
00:05:52,583 --> 00:05:53,583
What happened?

54
00:05:53,625 --> 00:05:55,291
Why so sluggish today?

55
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,875
Aren't you going to the station today?

56
00:05:58,916 --> 00:06:00,500
What's wrong? Aren't you feeling well?

57
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:02,708
Didn't sleep well.

58
00:06:05,458 --> 00:06:06,583
Let me guess.

59
00:06:06,708 --> 00:06:08,375
You dreamt about Pathu, didn't you?

60
00:06:08,416 --> 00:06:10,125
[soft music playing]

61
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:12,833
This is nothing new, Ajeeb.

62
00:06:12,916 --> 00:06:14,166
How long has it been?

63
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,583
She must be living happily somewhere.

64
00:06:21,291 --> 00:06:23,250
Let's just believe that.

65
00:06:25,708 --> 00:06:28,000
Don't ruin your morning
worrying about all this.

66
00:06:28,666 --> 00:06:30,708
Go get ready quickly.

67
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:32,291
You have parade today, right?

68
00:06:36,333 --> 00:06:37,458
Oh, by the way,

69
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,958
I'll be late today.
Could you pick me up from the bookstall?

70
00:06:39,958 --> 00:06:41,541
Is it okay if I come after my shift?

71
00:06:41,625 --> 00:06:43,375
Will you come or make me wait as usual?

72
00:06:43,416 --> 00:06:44,583
What kind of question is that?

73
00:06:44,625 --> 00:06:46,125
Have I ever made you wait?

74
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:47,208
Hmmm...

75
00:06:47,416 --> 00:06:48,708
I'm used to it by now.

76
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:53,333
[soft music playing]

77
00:07:00,125 --> 00:07:02,375
Yes, sir.
We're preparing for the parade here.

78
00:07:02,583 --> 00:07:03,875
How are you feeling now, sir?

79
00:07:04,083 --> 00:07:05,125
Is that so?

80
00:07:05,166 --> 00:07:06,166
Get well soon, sir.

81
00:07:06,208 --> 00:07:08,083
I always get to know
everything from you first.

82
00:07:08,166 --> 00:07:09,416
It was the SHO who called.

83
00:07:09,458 --> 00:07:11,333
The doctor advised a month's rest for him.

84
00:07:11,625 --> 00:07:15,333
I suspect someone
must have done this intentionally.

85
00:07:15,625 --> 00:07:17,416
No, that's highly unlikely.

86
00:07:17,625 --> 00:07:19,750
Luckily no vehicle came from
the opposite direction.

87
00:07:19,791 --> 00:07:22,833
By the way, the Thalassery SHO is
taking charge of this station for a month.

88
00:07:24,625 --> 00:07:26,083
Leelamma, make it quick.

89
00:07:26,083 --> 00:07:27,125
Yes, sir.

90
00:07:27,958 --> 00:07:29,416
The last vehicle has arrived!

91
00:07:29,541 --> 00:07:30,666
Okay, whatever.

92
00:07:30,916 --> 00:07:33,125
Hey, the tailor you mentioned yesterday...

93
00:07:33,125 --> 00:07:34,500
He's really good.

94
00:07:34,583 --> 00:07:36,875
The blouse he stitched yesterday
was perfect.

95
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,583
Didn't I tell you he's good?

96
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,416
Oh, was he the one you were talking about?

97
00:07:40,833 --> 00:07:42,458
But his charges are quite high.

98
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,458
[motorcycle passing]

99
00:07:48,208 --> 00:07:49,416
I'll be right there.

100
00:07:49,875 --> 00:07:51,750
No, I won't be late.

101
00:07:52,541 --> 00:07:53,750
Ajeeb sir is here.

102
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:55,333
Let's get ready for the parade.

103
00:07:57,916 --> 00:07:59,708
Ajeeb, you know we've parade on Fridays.

104
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,625
If we're late,
won't the constables learn from that?

105
00:08:01,666 --> 00:08:03,125
-Sorry, sir.
-Where your cap?

106
00:08:03,166 --> 00:08:04,958
-I'll go get it right now.
-Go get it.

107
00:08:05,458 --> 00:08:06,416
So, about the parade--

108
00:08:06,458 --> 00:08:07,791
Sir, shall I go and come?

109
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:09,583
Yes. Return immediately
once the hospital visit is done.

110
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:10,916
Okay.

111
00:08:10,958 --> 00:08:12,833
[upbeat music playing]

112
00:08:16,083 --> 00:08:17,291
Parade.

113
00:08:17,708 --> 00:08:18,750
Attention!

114
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,583
Officers, fall out.

115
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,500
Parade.

116
00:08:27,708 --> 00:08:29,375
Stand at ease.

117
00:08:30,583 --> 00:08:32,833
Sir, shouldn't we dispatch
the traffic duty officers?

118
00:08:32,875 --> 00:08:33,958
We will.

119
00:08:34,166 --> 00:08:36,625
Tressing by the right.

120
00:08:38,375 --> 00:08:39,583
Do it properly, Sunil.

121
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:40,750
As you are.

122
00:08:40,875 --> 00:08:43,500
Tressing by the right.

123
00:08:47,958 --> 00:08:49,750
[ambulance siren wailing]

124
00:08:56,958 --> 00:08:58,458
<i>-Fathima, Shafeeq.</i>
-They're calling us.

125
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:02,833
<i>Come in.</i>

126
00:09:05,916 --> 00:09:07,041
Haven't they called?

127
00:09:07,041 --> 00:09:08,708
You were supposed to come
before the test?

128
00:09:08,708 --> 00:09:10,125
Ah, so it's over?

129
00:09:10,250 --> 00:09:12,166
It's over. Where were you?

130
00:09:13,083 --> 00:09:17,125
Since you can't travel by bike,
I went home to get the car.

131
00:09:17,416 --> 00:09:19,375
I swear. That's why I'm late, my dear.

132
00:09:19,958 --> 00:09:21,875
Please let it be positive this time, Lord.

133
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:22,958
Molly Joy.

134
00:09:22,958 --> 00:09:24,500
-They called. Let's go.
-Okay.

135
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:33,875
Usually, the success rate is
90% after this treatment.

136
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,625
But...

137
00:09:37,875 --> 00:09:39,041
I am sorry.

138
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:41,208
Your test results are not positive.

139
00:09:41,291 --> 00:09:43,250
[soft music playing]

140
00:09:44,666 --> 00:09:48,916
Is there any specific reason for it?

141
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:51,500
Age is a factor.

142
00:09:51,666 --> 00:09:53,916
But in some cases,
it can still turn positive.

143
00:09:55,708 --> 00:09:56,958
Don't worry.

144
00:09:57,208 --> 00:09:59,000
We'll continue the treatment.

145
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:01,083
Let's wait for three months.

146
00:10:01,583 --> 00:10:03,750
Her haemoglobin level is slightly low.

147
00:10:04,041 --> 00:10:06,250
And there's a Vitamin D deficiency too.

148
00:10:06,791 --> 00:10:09,416
Anyway, I'm prescribing some medicines.

149
00:10:10,083 --> 00:10:11,333
Take them.

150
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:13,583
Let's see how it goes.
I'll see you during your next check-up.

151
00:10:13,625 --> 00:10:15,083
-Okay, Doctor.
-Alright, then.

152
00:10:15,208 --> 00:10:17,458
[melancholic music playing]

153
00:10:21,166 --> 00:10:23,083
[child giggling]

154
00:10:33,125 --> 00:10:34,875
Did you pick up the clothes
from the laundry?

155
00:10:34,875 --> 00:10:36,791
Oh no, I forgot about it.

156
00:10:37,208 --> 00:10:38,958
You always forget everything!

157
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,041
Don't pinch! It hurts!

158
00:10:41,083 --> 00:10:42,416
Don't we have to pick it up?

159
00:10:42,458 --> 00:10:43,833
We'll pick it up on the way.

160
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,291
Oh Lord...

161
00:10:45,375 --> 00:10:48,083
the way she tortures me
for every little thing!

162
00:10:48,833 --> 00:10:50,041
Sir...

163
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:51,833
We have two children.

164
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:54,083
A son and a daughter.

165
00:10:54,708 --> 00:10:56,458
Our daughter is in Bhopal.

166
00:10:56,541 --> 00:10:57,833
With her husband.

167
00:10:58,958 --> 00:11:01,333
Since the last several months,

168
00:11:02,083 --> 00:11:05,708
our son has been forcing us
to sell our house.

169
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:08,416
And yesterday, over this issue,

170
00:11:08,875 --> 00:11:11,583
he ended up beating him up, sir.

171
00:11:11,625 --> 00:11:13,041
[sobbing]

172
00:11:14,416 --> 00:11:17,000
Sir, where will we go
if we sell that house?

173
00:11:17,541 --> 00:11:19,791
Please call and talk to him, sir.

174
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:23,208
Don't worry.

175
00:11:23,375 --> 00:11:24,583
We will sort this out.

176
00:11:25,583 --> 00:11:26,791
Madhu sir...

177
00:11:27,791 --> 00:11:28,833
Madhu sir...

178
00:11:28,875 --> 00:11:30,750
My name is Madhu.

179
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,000
Yes...

180
00:11:33,625 --> 00:11:35,500
Listen, how do you say
'I'll call later' in Hindi?

181
00:11:35,541 --> 00:11:37,625
-Who knows!
-You don't know either?

182
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:43,291
I will... call you after some time.

183
00:11:43,541 --> 00:11:44,583
What the...

184
00:11:44,583 --> 00:11:45,666
My...

185
00:11:46,041 --> 00:11:48,041
Police station... is outside...

186
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:49,791
Madhu sir.

187
00:11:50,041 --> 00:11:51,458
-Give me the phone.
-Sorry, sir.

188
00:11:51,541 --> 00:11:53,000
Get a written complaint from them.

189
00:11:53,375 --> 00:11:54,375
I'll look into this.

190
00:11:54,875 --> 00:11:56,041
-Come with me.
-Hello.

191
00:11:56,291 --> 00:11:58,291
[In Hindi] I am the SI. Tell me.

192
00:11:59,291 --> 00:12:01,833
Manoj,
get their complaint in writing, okay?

193
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:02,875
Note down the number.

194
00:12:02,875 --> 00:12:03,916
Belluru?

195
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,500
Burnt body...

196
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Man missing.

197
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,208
Tell me the case number.

198
00:12:12,875 --> 00:12:13,875
Okay.

199
00:12:13,916 --> 00:12:15,208
83/23.

200
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:16,458
Age?

201
00:12:21,666 --> 00:12:22,916
Dharmadom?

202
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:27,750
Alright. We'll contact you
if we get any information.

203
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:28,916
Okay.

204
00:12:29,625 --> 00:12:30,750
-Madhu sir...
-Yes, sir.

205
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:33,250
There are more people from other states
than Malayalis now.

206
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:35,583
You'll struggle
if you don't learn some Hindi now.

207
00:12:36,458 --> 00:12:37,541
Renjith...

208
00:12:37,541 --> 00:12:39,500
-Look into the details of that case.
-Okay, sir.

209
00:12:39,583 --> 00:12:40,958
-Sir.
-Get the vehicle.

210
00:12:41,041 --> 00:12:42,083
Sir.

211
00:12:43,625 --> 00:12:45,375
-Sir, are you done?
-Yes, sir.

212
00:12:45,583 --> 00:12:47,416
Then please help them into that vehicle.

213
00:12:47,875 --> 00:12:49,416
They will drop you home, okay?

214
00:12:49,666 --> 00:12:50,791
Alright.

215
00:12:51,083 --> 00:12:52,583
[cheerful music playing]

216
00:12:53,416 --> 00:12:55,125
[motorcycle passing]

217
00:12:56,458 --> 00:12:59,125
[cheerful music playing]

218
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:05,416
Never arrive on time, okay?

219
00:13:05,458 --> 00:13:07,250
Something came up
just when I was about to leave.

220
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:08,666
Isn't it like this every time?

221
00:13:08,875 --> 00:13:11,166
Get on. We'll go home and fight.

222
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:21,708
-Where did you go at this hour?
-Just for a ride, sir.

223
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:23,166
-What's in the bike?
-Nothing.

224
00:13:23,208 --> 00:13:25,291
-Where are the papers?
-I've got them, sir.

225
00:13:25,291 --> 00:13:26,916
-Have you smoked weed, man?
-No sir, I don't smoke.

226
00:13:26,916 --> 00:13:28,375
-Have you?
-No, sir.

227
00:13:28,416 --> 00:13:29,875
-Are you telling the truth?
-Maybe.

228
00:13:29,916 --> 00:13:31,125
Show me your license.

229
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:33,625
-Well sir, I forgot...
-Go tell that to the SI.

230
00:13:33,666 --> 00:13:34,958
-Go on.
-Sir, please...

231
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,125
Move it, man!

232
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,083
Joy sir...

233
00:13:38,833 --> 00:13:40,041
Sir!

234
00:13:40,125 --> 00:13:41,541
Sleeping like a log!

235
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,166
What is it, Renjith?

236
00:13:44,416 --> 00:13:46,000
Sir, they aren't drunk.

237
00:13:46,083 --> 00:13:47,541
But something feels off about them.

238
00:13:47,583 --> 00:13:49,083
-What are you guys up to?
-Nothing...

239
00:13:49,208 --> 00:13:51,416
If so, couldn't you just sit at home?
Where did you go?

240
00:13:51,458 --> 00:13:53,208
We just stepped out for a tea, sir.

241
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:54,375
What do you guys do?

242
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,083
Sir... he is a film actor.

243
00:13:56,791 --> 00:13:58,166
-Yes, sir.
-Who, him?

244
00:13:59,250 --> 00:14:01,250
-In which movie?
-"Dhurandham" (Disaster).

245
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:03,416
There's no such film, sir.

246
00:14:03,416 --> 00:14:04,583
It's yet to be released, sir.

247
00:14:04,625 --> 00:14:06,958
Why don't you call yourself an actor
after it releases?

248
00:14:07,375 --> 00:14:08,416
That would've been better.

249
00:14:08,458 --> 00:14:10,916
Anyway, get out of here
before this turns into a real disaster.

250
00:14:11,041 --> 00:14:12,625
Get their number and details
and let them go.

251
00:14:12,625 --> 00:14:13,583
Alright, sir.

252
00:14:15,083 --> 00:14:17,791
[soft music playing]

253
00:14:30,708 --> 00:14:32,500
[phone ringing]

254
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:36,708
Hello, this is the police station.

255
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:38,333
Where?

256
00:14:38,375 --> 00:14:40,375
<i>Exhale deeply and try stretching</i>

257
00:14:40,375 --> 00:14:42,791
<i>-your entire body forward.</i>
-Oh, my goodness...

258
00:14:43,125 --> 00:14:45,708
<i>Once more,
stretch a little further forward.</i>

259
00:14:47,208 --> 00:14:49,458
I'm trying... I'm trying...
It's my stomach.

260
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:52,541
Once this reduces a bit, I can do it.

261
00:14:52,583 --> 00:14:54,708
-I've started walking now.
<i>-A bit more.</i>

262
00:14:54,708 --> 00:14:55,833
I'll do it...

263
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,250
[phone ringing]

264
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,708
Thank God for the bell!

265
00:14:59,166 --> 00:15:01,291
Teacher, it's from the station.
I'll do it tomorrow.

266
00:15:03,291 --> 00:15:04,666
Sir, we got an information.

267
00:15:04,708 --> 00:15:07,708
Someone called about a dead body
in an abandoned well at Koduvally.

268
00:15:07,916 --> 00:15:09,125
Dead body?

269
00:15:09,125 --> 00:15:10,916
-Man or woman?
-Don't know, sir.

270
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:13,333
-Do you have the location?
-Yes, sir.

271
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,916
Who all are at the station now?

272
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:16,791
Only night-duty officers are here.

273
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:19,666
Take whoever's there
and head to the spot.

274
00:15:19,708 --> 00:15:20,625
Okay, sir.

275
00:15:20,666 --> 00:15:22,500
Call me once you reach there
and update me.

276
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,125
I'll join you once
I'm done with the daily reporting.

277
00:15:24,166 --> 00:15:25,375
Okay, sir.

278
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:26,791
What a day to start!

279
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:28,541
Wonder whose face I saw first this morning.

280
00:15:28,583 --> 00:15:29,916
It must be Teacher's.
Who else?

281
00:15:30,166 --> 00:15:32,166
PART TWO
SHOBHA - THE VICTIM

282
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:34,958
[police siren wailing]

283
00:15:40,458 --> 00:15:42,000
It's packed with people here.

284
00:15:42,125 --> 00:15:43,333
We'll clear them out, sir.

285
00:15:49,625 --> 00:15:51,666
[indistinct crowd chatter]

286
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:56,458
Move away.

287
00:15:57,416 --> 00:15:58,625
Step back.

288
00:15:58,666 --> 00:15:59,916
Move aside, everyone.

289
00:15:59,958 --> 00:16:01,125
-Step aside.
-Come on, move!

290
00:16:01,166 --> 00:16:03,000
-Make way for , sir.
-Move!

291
00:16:03,083 --> 00:16:04,083
Sir.

292
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:07,416
[mysterious music playing]

293
00:16:13,166 --> 00:16:14,416
Move everyone back.

294
00:16:14,416 --> 00:16:16,166
Please step back, all of you.

295
00:16:16,208 --> 00:16:17,291
I...

296
00:16:17,333 --> 00:16:18,583
I'll call Nandakumar , sir.

297
00:16:18,625 --> 00:16:19,625
Okay.

298
00:16:19,958 --> 00:16:21,666
Looks like it's been two or three days.

299
00:16:30,375 --> 00:16:31,458
Move.

300
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,000
Sir, body is in the well.

301
00:16:38,041 --> 00:16:38,958
And?

302
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
It's very deep.

303
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,833
-Did you inform the fire force?
-Not yet, sir.

304
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,208
Then you get down and bring it up!

305
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:44,166
Sir...

306
00:16:44,166 --> 00:16:46,625
-Call the fire force. Quick.
<i>-Okay, sir.</i>

307
00:16:46,625 --> 00:16:48,625
Don't you know these basic things?

308
00:16:48,666 --> 00:16:50,333
Ajeeb, use your head.
Do what's needed.

309
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:51,958
Call the photographer too.

310
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,666
Okay, sir.
I'll call them right away.

311
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:56,708
<i>P20 mobile control room.</i>

312
00:16:56,708 --> 00:16:58,000
Dharmadom PS answering.

313
00:16:58,125 --> 00:16:59,250
Good morning, sir.

314
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:00,416
Over.

315
00:17:00,875 --> 00:17:03,208
Sir, seventeen cases have been reported.

316
00:17:03,625 --> 00:17:05,291
Four suo moto cases have been taken.

317
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:07,583
Under 185, six cases have been registered.

318
00:17:07,708 --> 00:17:09,458
[suspenseful music playing]

319
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:12,250
<i>As you can see,
we are at the scene of the incident.</i>

320
00:17:13,458 --> 00:17:17,458
<i>We will soon find out
if this was a suicide or an accident.</i>

321
00:17:18,708 --> 00:17:19,666
-Sir.
-Hi, sir.

322
00:17:19,666 --> 00:17:20,916
It's a woman's body.

323
00:17:20,958 --> 00:17:22,208
It's quite decomposed.

324
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,333
Move... Move...

325
00:17:39,041 --> 00:17:40,375
Media, to the side.

326
00:17:40,375 --> 00:17:41,708
Move back!

327
00:17:42,208 --> 00:17:43,833
Please stay back.

328
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,666
Don't crowd around.
Move back.

329
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:00,291
Hold it.

330
00:18:00,291 --> 00:18:01,625
Can't you hear?

331
00:18:07,875 --> 00:18:10,166
-Tighten it... Hold on...
-Move, move.

332
00:18:10,208 --> 00:18:11,875
-Move back!
-Step back...

333
00:18:18,458 --> 00:18:21,166
[suspenseful music playing]

334
00:18:37,958 --> 00:18:39,291
[retching]

335
00:18:39,416 --> 00:18:40,583
-Sir...
-Okay, sir.

336
00:18:46,916 --> 00:18:48,708
Sir... Are you okay?

337
00:18:48,916 --> 00:18:50,500
-I'm okay, I'm okay...
-Here...

338
00:18:52,333 --> 00:18:54,041
It's because it's your first time, sir.

339
00:18:54,041 --> 00:18:55,583
Don't worry, you'll get used to it.

340
00:18:55,625 --> 00:18:57,875
Sir, since it's a female body,
we'll need woman officers.

341
00:18:57,875 --> 00:18:59,750
They're coming with Nandakumar , sir.

342
00:19:03,916 --> 00:19:04,958
Move everyone back.

343
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,791
We'll need a screen for the inquest, right?

344
00:19:07,583 --> 00:19:10,125
Move the people away
and line up the vehicles around.

345
00:19:10,125 --> 00:19:11,708
Okay, sir.
Everyone, back up!

346
00:19:11,916 --> 00:19:13,750
Sir, can you call the photographer?

347
00:19:14,041 --> 00:19:15,708
[police siren wailing]

348
00:19:18,083 --> 00:19:19,416
Move aside.

349
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,791
Don't push... Move... Keep moving.

350
00:19:22,166 --> 00:19:23,458
Move over there.

351
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,375
Everyone to the side.

352
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,916
-What's happening, Ajeeb?
-We've called the photographer.

353
00:19:28,916 --> 00:19:29,958
He'll be here soon.

354
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,625
It's a woman's body, sir.
Looks like it's a few days old.

355
00:19:33,666 --> 00:19:34,833
Stay back.

356
00:19:34,833 --> 00:19:36,541
Don't come this side.

357
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:39,125
What a stench...

358
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,625
Move.

359
00:19:45,208 --> 00:19:48,083
Don't stand around.
Keep moving.

360
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:50,375
-Where were you?
-Had a Save-the-date shoot, sir.

361
00:19:50,416 --> 00:19:51,500
Go on.

362
00:19:53,041 --> 00:19:54,166
Greetings, sir.

363
00:19:54,416 --> 00:19:55,666
Quick. Take the pictures.

364
00:19:55,833 --> 00:19:57,083
Sir, the ambulance is almost here.

365
00:19:57,083 --> 00:19:58,291
Sir, we're leaving.

366
00:19:58,541 --> 00:19:59,791
Work's done.

367
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:01,291
-Alright, sir. See you.
-Okay, then.

368
00:20:04,416 --> 00:20:06,083
Jose, take the breadth.

369
00:20:07,208 --> 00:20:09,041
Look at Joy.
He knows the work.

370
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:10,125
Sir.

371
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:11,375
Watch and learn.

372
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:13,291
Note it down.
Make a sketch too.

373
00:20:14,083 --> 00:20:15,250
Now take the length.

374
00:20:16,625 --> 00:20:17,958
Hold it away.

375
00:20:18,541 --> 00:20:20,250
Now the head part.

376
00:20:20,916 --> 00:20:22,083
Take a picture of it.

377
00:20:22,083 --> 00:20:23,166
Okay, sir.

378
00:20:32,458 --> 00:20:33,625
[camera shutter clicking]

379
00:20:34,083 --> 00:20:35,833
[police jeep approaching]

380
00:20:36,375 --> 00:20:38,583
Move aside.
Close the door.

381
00:20:47,041 --> 00:20:48,958
Enough, Ajeeb.
It's been so long.

382
00:20:48,958 --> 00:20:50,666
You've been doing this
since you got back.

383
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:51,875
Stop it.

384
00:20:54,041 --> 00:20:55,291
No matter how much I wash,

385
00:20:55,291 --> 00:20:56,583
the smell won't go.

386
00:20:56,958 --> 00:20:58,083
Let me see.

387
00:20:59,375 --> 00:21:00,583
Right?

388
00:21:00,791 --> 00:21:02,500
No... nothing.

389
00:21:02,791 --> 00:21:04,541
You're imagining it.
There's no smell.

390
00:21:05,166 --> 00:21:06,583
[doorbell ringing]

391
00:21:06,708 --> 00:21:07,916
Who's that now?

392
00:21:08,208 --> 00:21:09,416
I'll check.

393
00:21:15,208 --> 00:21:16,375
Ah, look who's here!

394
00:21:16,666 --> 00:21:17,916
Please come in..

395
00:21:17,916 --> 00:21:19,416
What brings you here at this hour?

396
00:21:19,583 --> 00:21:21,208
Got something for you.
Go on, give it.

397
00:21:21,541 --> 00:21:23,375
-What's this?
-Biryani.

398
00:21:23,458 --> 00:21:25,041
I'm not bragging...

399
00:21:25,166 --> 00:21:28,125
No one makes biriyani like she does.

400
00:21:28,416 --> 00:21:29,583
You needn't flatter me.

401
00:21:30,166 --> 00:21:31,166
Here.

402
00:21:31,208 --> 00:21:34,000
Oh, but we already made dinner.

403
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:35,666
That's alright.
Have it tomorrow.

404
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:37,708
But don't miss 'Molly' biriyani.

405
00:21:38,250 --> 00:21:39,666
Did Uppa eat?

406
00:21:39,750 --> 00:21:41,750
Since he has medicines to take,
he eats early.

407
00:21:42,208 --> 00:21:43,916
Sir... 'Molly' Biryani for you!

408
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:46,333
Why are you standing?
Please sit.

409
00:21:46,375 --> 00:21:47,833
We brought some biryani.

410
00:21:48,416 --> 00:21:49,541
Smells amazing.

411
00:21:52,416 --> 00:21:54,333
I don't want...
I can't eat anything now.

412
00:21:55,333 --> 00:21:56,291
[phone ringing]

413
00:21:56,291 --> 00:21:57,333
What happened to him?

414
00:21:57,333 --> 00:22:00,000
Don't ask. He's been like this
since he got back from the station.

415
00:22:00,041 --> 00:22:01,041
Didn't even have his tea.

416
00:22:01,083 --> 00:22:02,291
-Oh, dear...
-Ah...

417
00:22:02,416 --> 00:22:03,958
-Now I get it.
<i>-Hello, sir?</i>

418
00:22:04,041 --> 00:22:05,500
It'll pass after a while.

419
00:22:05,583 --> 00:22:07,333
Eventually, he'll get used to it.

420
00:22:08,041 --> 00:22:09,166
Shall we go?

421
00:22:09,291 --> 00:22:10,833
-Alright, then goodnight.
-Bye.

422
00:22:11,125 --> 00:22:12,416
Oh, okay.

423
00:22:13,291 --> 00:22:14,916
That's fine, sir.
I'll be right there.

424
00:22:16,791 --> 00:22:18,333
I need to go to the station.

425
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:19,583
What? You're going now?

426
00:22:19,583 --> 00:22:20,958
Don't you ever get any rest?

427
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:22,500
No rest for a probationary SI.

428
00:22:23,083 --> 00:22:24,333
Can you make me a lime tea?

429
00:22:24,375 --> 00:22:25,708
-Okay.
-I'll get ready and come.

430
00:22:26,583 --> 00:22:28,041
[motorcycle passing]

431
00:22:30,583 --> 00:22:32,208
[mysterious music playing]

432
00:22:40,625 --> 00:22:41,750
Ajeeb...

433
00:22:41,958 --> 00:22:43,583
No one has identified the body yet.

434
00:22:44,083 --> 00:22:45,750
Since it's a woman's body,

435
00:22:45,791 --> 00:22:48,166
we can't just file it under Section 174
and close the case.

436
00:22:48,833 --> 00:22:50,458
What did the doctor say after the inquest?

437
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:52,416
Sir, according to the inquest,
it's death by drowning.

438
00:22:52,875 --> 00:22:55,583
There are no signs of
struggle or sexual assault on the body.

439
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:58,958
Prima facie, it is likely to be a suicide.

440
00:23:00,291 --> 00:23:02,791
Chances are no one will come
looking for her.

441
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:05,166
Even so,
shouldn't someone identify the body?

442
00:23:08,625 --> 00:23:09,791
What language is this?

443
00:23:11,375 --> 00:23:12,375
Telugu?

444
00:23:12,375 --> 00:23:13,416
It's Kannada, sir.

445
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:16,625
We need to check
all the recent missing women cases

446
00:23:16,666 --> 00:23:18,208
reported in our district.

447
00:23:18,250 --> 00:23:19,250
Sir.

448
00:23:19,416 --> 00:23:21,375
Tomorrow, conduct an inquiry
around that area.

449
00:23:21,750 --> 00:23:24,833
Take Joy or someone else along
depending on their duty.

450
00:23:24,875 --> 00:23:25,875
Alright, sir.

451
00:23:29,291 --> 00:23:31,583
I checked the missing
women cases in the district,

452
00:23:31,875 --> 00:23:33,666
nothing matches this one.

453
00:23:34,708 --> 00:23:38,375
We have a lot of Tamilians, Bengalis,
and Kannadigas living here.

454
00:23:39,083 --> 00:23:41,583
Their missing cases often go unreported.

455
00:23:42,916 --> 00:23:46,333
Since there are no complainants,
it's possible she was a nomad.

456
00:23:47,250 --> 00:23:49,333
Didn't you notice the tattoo on her arm?

457
00:23:50,083 --> 00:23:52,166
And, isn't this an area where nomads stay?

458
00:23:53,125 --> 00:23:56,208
I thought we could ask around,
but there's no one in sight.

459
00:23:59,666 --> 00:24:00,833
Please stop the vehicle, sir.

460
00:24:00,916 --> 00:24:02,750
Ustad, please come here.

461
00:24:04,625 --> 00:24:05,958
We are from the Dharmadom police station.

462
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:06,958
What's the matter, sir?

463
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,125
Do you live nearby?

464
00:24:08,291 --> 00:24:10,583
Yes, barely half a kilometre from here.

465
00:24:10,625 --> 00:24:11,583
Ustad...

466
00:24:11,583 --> 00:24:13,458
Do you know any of the nomads

467
00:24:13,458 --> 00:24:16,083
or migrant workers living around here?

468
00:24:16,125 --> 00:24:17,416
I don't know them personally.

469
00:24:17,416 --> 00:24:19,041
When I go to the mosque
for the morning prayers,

470
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,375
I hear a lot of commotion.

471
00:24:20,416 --> 00:24:23,208
And when I return at night,
I've seen their children playing.

472
00:24:24,041 --> 00:24:25,000
Alright then.

473
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:26,208
Okay, sir.

474
00:24:27,541 --> 00:24:28,666
Let's go.

475
00:24:28,791 --> 00:24:31,541
[background announcement]

476
00:24:33,916 --> 00:24:35,958
Family Health Centre.

477
00:24:36,250 --> 00:24:37,375
Kolassery.

478
00:24:39,416 --> 00:24:42,250
Sir, the list will be ready only
after the polio vaccine is distributed.

479
00:24:42,416 --> 00:24:44,791
Currently we're conducting
the awareness program.

480
00:24:45,166 --> 00:24:48,625
ASHA workers and Anganwadi staff
are the ones handling that part.

481
00:24:48,791 --> 00:24:49,625
Okay.

482
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:50,833
One minute, sir.

483
00:24:51,208 --> 00:24:52,208
Prameela...

484
00:24:52,208 --> 00:24:53,333
Yes?

485
00:24:53,791 --> 00:24:54,875
I'll be right back.

486
00:24:55,916 --> 00:24:58,083
Prameela, this is our station SI.

487
00:24:58,750 --> 00:24:59,875
What is it, sir?

488
00:24:59,916 --> 00:25:02,208
Do you collect the details of
everyone in this area

489
00:25:02,208 --> 00:25:03,708
as part of the polio drive?

490
00:25:03,750 --> 00:25:04,791
Yes, sir.

491
00:25:04,791 --> 00:25:07,208
Right now, we are collecting
the details of those who have children.

492
00:25:07,250 --> 00:25:09,375
What about the migrants from other states?

493
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,791
We collect theirs too.

494
00:25:10,875 --> 00:25:12,208
I need those details.

495
00:25:17,541 --> 00:25:18,625
Here it is, sir.

496
00:25:19,041 --> 00:25:22,083
Most of these people in the list
live in Koduvally area.

497
00:25:22,416 --> 00:25:23,750
All the details are in here.

498
00:25:23,791 --> 00:25:24,875
Alright.

499
00:25:24,916 --> 00:25:27,125
[mysterious music playing]

500
00:25:32,083 --> 00:25:33,375
-Okay. Thank you.
-Alright, sir.

501
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:44,083
How is your CI now?

502
00:25:44,375 --> 00:25:47,083
They said he'll have to rest
until his arm heals.

503
00:25:47,416 --> 00:25:49,541
-What happened to that 174 case?
-Under investigation, sir.

504
00:25:49,541 --> 00:25:52,083
Since they are nomads,
we haven't gotten much info yet.

505
00:25:52,125 --> 00:25:54,250
I already have enough headache here.

506
00:25:54,250 --> 00:25:55,333
You know that, right?

507
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:57,000
You are on probation, aren't you?

508
00:25:57,166 --> 00:25:58,125
Yes, sir.

509
00:25:58,125 --> 00:26:00,208
Nandakumar, let him handle this then.

510
00:26:00,208 --> 00:26:01,125
Sir.

511
00:26:01,125 --> 00:26:02,250
Just monitor it.

512
00:26:02,250 --> 00:26:03,208
Sir.

513
00:26:03,208 --> 00:26:05,375
If there's anything to sign or approve,
let me know.

514
00:26:05,375 --> 00:26:06,416
-Alright, sir.
-Okay.

515
00:26:11,708 --> 00:26:13,541
[motorcycle passing]

516
00:26:16,791 --> 00:26:18,291
Have you been waiting for long, sir?

517
00:26:18,291 --> 00:26:19,583
No, I just got here.

518
00:26:22,166 --> 00:26:24,375
[upbeat music playing]

519
00:26:29,166 --> 00:26:30,208
Joy sir...

520
00:26:30,250 --> 00:26:32,333
If you cover this side,
I'll take care of the rest.

521
00:26:34,750 --> 00:26:38,000
Do you know anything about the nomad woman
who died here recently?

522
00:26:38,166 --> 00:26:39,541
How long have you been staying here?

523
00:26:39,583 --> 00:26:40,750
Three years.

524
00:26:40,750 --> 00:26:42,083
Anybody from Karnataka living here?

525
00:26:42,125 --> 00:26:43,791
-Don't know, sir.
-What do you do?

526
00:26:44,166 --> 00:26:45,208
What do you do?

527
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:46,666
I am a daily wage worker.

528
00:26:46,791 --> 00:26:49,250
Any Kannadigas living here
who are into construction work?

529
00:26:49,375 --> 00:26:51,458
Are you staying here? Since when?

530
00:26:51,708 --> 00:26:52,916
They live there.

531
00:26:52,916 --> 00:26:54,166
Oh, is that so?

532
00:26:54,375 --> 00:26:55,416
Sir.

533
00:26:56,083 --> 00:26:57,875
[upbeat music playing]

534
00:26:57,916 --> 00:26:59,541
Sir, this is where they live.

535
00:27:02,250 --> 00:27:03,333
Hello.

536
00:27:05,375 --> 00:27:07,000
I am the SI of the local station.

537
00:27:07,083 --> 00:27:08,041
My name is Ajeeb.

538
00:27:08,083 --> 00:27:09,083
What is your name?

539
00:27:09,083 --> 00:27:10,250
Durga.

540
00:27:10,708 --> 00:27:12,333
How long have you been staying here?

541
00:27:12,875 --> 00:27:14,625
Around six months, sir.

542
00:27:15,083 --> 00:27:16,250
And your native?

543
00:27:17,291 --> 00:27:18,625
Virajpet.

544
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:21,791
Are you aware a woman's body
was found here recently?

545
00:27:21,916 --> 00:27:24,208
I heard everyone talking about it, sir.

546
00:27:24,791 --> 00:27:26,666
Everyone was talking about it,
that's when I found out.

547
00:27:26,708 --> 00:27:28,125
Did you know her?

548
00:27:28,125 --> 00:27:29,166
No, sir.

549
00:27:29,416 --> 00:27:31,125
I saw you lingering around the spot

550
00:27:31,166 --> 00:27:32,791
where the body was found that day.

551
00:27:33,083 --> 00:27:34,125
Tell us the truth.

552
00:27:34,166 --> 00:27:35,791
Don't you know the dead woman?

553
00:27:36,333 --> 00:27:37,500
No, sir.

554
00:27:37,625 --> 00:27:39,333
Why are you lying?

555
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:43,708
The thing is, sir...
my younger sister got a job in Dubai.

556
00:27:43,875 --> 00:27:45,500
Everyone here warned that

557
00:27:45,791 --> 00:27:48,666
if there's a police case,
it will be difficult to get the visa.

558
00:27:49,041 --> 00:27:50,416
Out of that fear...

559
00:27:50,458 --> 00:27:52,208
Let the truth come out,

560
00:27:52,208 --> 00:27:54,166
I'll show you what Dubai is.

561
00:27:55,458 --> 00:27:56,666
What was her name?

562
00:27:56,708 --> 00:27:58,291
-Shobha.
-Shobha?

563
00:27:59,750 --> 00:28:01,083
How do you know her?

564
00:28:01,208 --> 00:28:04,541
I met her when I went to work
at a construction site.

565
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:06,125
Do you know where Shobha was staying?

566
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:08,791
I don't know, sir.

567
00:28:08,791 --> 00:28:10,500
What else do you know about her?

568
00:28:11,666 --> 00:28:14,791
Shobha has two children.

569
00:28:15,208 --> 00:28:19,125
I saw them once
when she brought them to our work site.

570
00:28:19,666 --> 00:28:21,916
Also, she mentioned once that

571
00:28:21,916 --> 00:28:25,291
her husband was working
somewhere near Tumkur.

572
00:28:25,375 --> 00:28:27,541
Do you know
her or her husband's phone number?

573
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:31,458
No, sir.

574
00:28:31,708 --> 00:28:32,916
Here...

575
00:28:33,208 --> 00:28:34,458
For us...

576
00:28:35,083 --> 00:28:37,000
If you want to know more than this,

577
00:28:37,041 --> 00:28:38,958
we have an agent who gives us jobs.

578
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,125
Sibu settan.

579
00:28:40,166 --> 00:28:41,208
Who? Huh?

580
00:28:41,208 --> 00:28:42,208
Sibu settan.

581
00:28:42,500 --> 00:28:44,708
Where can we find this "Sibu settan" now?

582
00:28:44,875 --> 00:28:48,333
Sir, there's a new building
under construction near the bus stand.

583
00:28:48,416 --> 00:28:49,958
He'll be there.

584
00:28:50,333 --> 00:28:52,500
If we find out that you're lying,

585
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:54,833
you will be summoned to the station.

586
00:28:54,916 --> 00:28:56,083
Understood?

587
00:28:58,416 --> 00:28:59,458
One more thing.

588
00:29:01,166 --> 00:29:03,041
Do you know what this tattoo says?

589
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:06,041
Read it out.

590
00:29:06,333 --> 00:29:07,375
Raju.

591
00:29:12,625 --> 00:29:14,458
Sir, you really scared the life out of her.

592
00:29:14,708 --> 00:29:16,625
This is how we survive in this job.

593
00:29:17,416 --> 00:29:19,500
[mysterious music playing]

594
00:29:29,291 --> 00:29:31,083
Can you recognise who this is, Shibu?

595
00:29:31,458 --> 00:29:33,583
Looks like Shobha, sir.

596
00:29:34,541 --> 00:29:36,125
How do you know her?

597
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:38,375
She used to come to the site for work, sir.

598
00:29:38,416 --> 00:29:39,875
When was the last time you saw her?

599
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:41,416
Must be around 10 days ago, sir.

600
00:29:41,666 --> 00:29:45,458
How can you be so sure that
it's been exactly 10 days?

601
00:29:45,500 --> 00:29:48,833
We started working at this site
only a week ago, sir.

602
00:29:49,208 --> 00:29:51,791
She last came to work
at our previous site.

603
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:55,250
What happened to her, sir?

604
00:29:55,291 --> 00:29:56,833
Do you have Shobha's phone number?

605
00:29:56,833 --> 00:29:58,083
Shobha doesn't own a phone, sir.

606
00:29:58,125 --> 00:30:00,125
Then how do you call her for work?

607
00:30:00,208 --> 00:30:02,250
She usually shows up at the site
in the morning.

608
00:30:02,625 --> 00:30:05,375
On days there is work, she finishes it,
collects her wages and leaves.

609
00:30:05,583 --> 00:30:08,125
So there's never a need to call them, sir.

610
00:30:09,375 --> 00:30:12,708
It was her husband
who first brought her for work.

611
00:30:12,833 --> 00:30:13,958
Do you know him?

612
00:30:13,958 --> 00:30:15,208
I don't really know him, sir.

613
00:30:15,250 --> 00:30:16,500
What does he do?

614
00:30:16,708 --> 00:30:19,375
He told me
he does something in movies, sir.

615
00:30:19,500 --> 00:30:20,500
Movies?

616
00:30:20,583 --> 00:30:21,958
I don't exactly remember.

617
00:30:22,875 --> 00:30:24,458
Could he be a film actor?

618
00:30:24,666 --> 00:30:26,666
[soft music playing]

619
00:30:28,500 --> 00:30:30,666
Have you seen this tattoo on her arm?

620
00:30:31,916 --> 00:30:33,208
I haven't noticed.

621
00:30:33,291 --> 00:30:34,916
Do you know what's written here?

622
00:30:36,083 --> 00:30:37,500
What language is this, sir?

623
00:30:40,375 --> 00:30:41,916
Where is Shobha's house?

624
00:30:42,166 --> 00:30:45,958
There's a railway line
slightly west of Koduvally.

625
00:30:46,541 --> 00:30:49,083
She lives in some wasteland area
just past that.

626
00:30:49,875 --> 00:30:51,416
Unlock your phone and give it to me.

627
00:30:58,750 --> 00:31:00,500
The last dialled number is mine.

628
00:31:00,625 --> 00:31:01,916
I'll call you if I need anything.

629
00:31:01,958 --> 00:31:03,041
Okay, sir.

630
00:31:07,416 --> 00:31:08,500
Sir...

631
00:31:09,750 --> 00:31:11,875
Her husband's name is Raju.

632
00:31:11,916 --> 00:31:14,500
[mysterious music playing]

633
00:31:38,416 --> 00:31:40,791
The well where the body was found is
right nearby, isn't it?

634
00:31:40,833 --> 00:31:42,083
Yeah, it's close by.

635
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:10,833
Didn't Durga say that Shobha had two kids?

636
00:32:12,083 --> 00:32:14,333
But I don't see
any of their belongings or clothes here.

637
00:32:33,250 --> 00:32:35,541
[train passing]

638
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:41,833
<i>Pathu, my child!</i>

639
00:32:43,250 --> 00:32:45,208
<i>Pathu!</i>

640
00:33:03,791 --> 00:33:04,916
Sir...

641
00:33:05,666 --> 00:33:07,625
Look, I found a photo.

642
00:33:10,375 --> 00:33:12,500
[rhythmic music playing]

643
00:33:15,208 --> 00:33:16,583
The kids are in it too.

644
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:20,041
So this must be Shobha.

645
00:33:32,708 --> 00:33:33,833
Mohan sir...

646
00:33:33,875 --> 00:33:35,958
How long will it take
to get the postmortem report?

647
00:33:36,083 --> 00:33:37,708
Sir, the report gets generated
the same day.

648
00:33:37,750 --> 00:33:39,958
Usually, the delay is in
getting the document typed.

649
00:33:40,375 --> 00:33:42,500
In normal cases,
we'd get it within 2-3 weeks.

650
00:33:42,583 --> 00:33:45,083
If we keep pushing them,
they'll give it within a week.

651
00:33:47,083 --> 00:33:49,083
Is it about that nomad woman's case?

652
00:33:49,125 --> 00:33:50,000
Yeah, that one.

653
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:52,041
My dear sir,
there's no point running after that.

654
00:33:52,083 --> 00:33:54,458
There are no complainants or witnesses
in this case.

655
00:33:54,458 --> 00:33:56,958
Even for cases which have these,
we're unable to finish the paperwork.

656
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,125
-Let alone this.
-Alright.

657
00:33:59,208 --> 00:34:02,166
Sir, someone's here to see you.
His name is Shibu.

658
00:34:02,208 --> 00:34:03,666
-Yeah, send him in.
-Come on in.

659
00:34:05,958 --> 00:34:07,416
-Sir...
-Yeah, come in.

660
00:34:09,041 --> 00:34:10,125
Have a seat.

661
00:34:13,041 --> 00:34:14,416
Why did you call for me, sir?

662
00:34:16,458 --> 00:34:17,958
Take a look and tell me who this is.

663
00:34:19,333 --> 00:34:20,666
This is Shobha, sir.

664
00:34:23,125 --> 00:34:24,291
So, who are these people?

665
00:34:26,583 --> 00:34:28,958
Isn't he a film actor, sir?

666
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:31,333
Not him,
who are the ones standing with him?

667
00:34:31,958 --> 00:34:33,375
That's Shobha's family, sir.

668
00:34:33,583 --> 00:34:35,458
You mean Shobha's husband and kids.
Correct?

669
00:34:35,625 --> 00:34:36,625
Yes, sir.

670
00:34:38,416 --> 00:34:39,958
So is this the Raju you mentioned?

671
00:34:40,125 --> 00:34:41,125
Yes.

672
00:34:43,958 --> 00:34:45,416
Alright, you may go.

673
00:34:46,125 --> 00:34:48,041
-I'll call you again if needed.
-Alright, sir.

674
00:34:51,291 --> 00:34:53,583
Since it's confirmed that
the body is Shobha's,

675
00:34:54,250 --> 00:34:55,541
what about her family?

676
00:34:55,666 --> 00:34:56,666
Any relatives?

677
00:34:56,708 --> 00:34:57,875
Sir, she has two kids.

678
00:34:57,916 --> 00:34:59,125
They are currently missing.

679
00:34:59,375 --> 00:35:01,250
And her husband
works in movies or something.

680
00:35:01,375 --> 00:35:02,958
He only visits occasionally.

681
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,375
His name is Raju, right?

682
00:35:04,416 --> 00:35:05,458
Yes, sir.

683
00:35:05,833 --> 00:35:07,083
Shouldn't he be informed?

684
00:35:07,166 --> 00:35:08,791
Do we have his address or phone number?

685
00:35:08,833 --> 00:35:12,208
It's been long since anyone saw him, sir.

686
00:35:12,208 --> 00:35:14,041
Doesn't seem like they were together.

687
00:35:14,083 --> 00:35:16,916
We found a photo
when we searched Shobha's house.

688
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,250
A family photo.

689
00:35:23,458 --> 00:35:25,166
The studio details are on it.

690
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:29,375
Good. Then do one thing.

691
00:35:29,625 --> 00:35:30,833
Go there.

692
00:35:31,041 --> 00:35:32,833
-If you find him, bring him here.
-Sir.

693
00:35:32,916 --> 00:35:34,875
Let's find out what he has to say.

694
00:35:34,958 --> 00:35:37,291
We also need to move the body
out of the mortuary soon.

695
00:35:37,333 --> 00:35:38,416
Yes, sir.

696
00:35:39,958 --> 00:35:42,041
You're going to another state.
Don't take any risks.

697
00:35:42,083 --> 00:35:43,791
Take someone experienced along with you.

698
00:35:43,833 --> 00:35:45,000
I'll take Joy sir with me, sir.

699
00:35:45,041 --> 00:35:46,291
Eh? Me?

700
00:35:46,333 --> 00:35:47,666
Yeah, that settles it.

701
00:35:48,333 --> 00:35:49,750
-Start the vehicle.
-But... I...

702
00:35:52,666 --> 00:35:53,666
Sir...

703
00:35:54,166 --> 00:35:57,083
It would have been helpful
if we could get the postmortem report soon.

704
00:35:57,708 --> 00:36:00,458
That liaison at the medical college...
What's his name?

705
00:36:00,500 --> 00:36:01,458
Antony.

706
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:02,708
Yes. Antony.

707
00:36:02,750 --> 00:36:03,958
I'll call and inform him.

708
00:36:04,083 --> 00:36:05,125
Sir.

709
00:36:05,458 --> 00:36:08,166
[jeep passing]

710
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:11,916
Was there really any need
to drag me into this?

711
00:36:12,041 --> 00:36:14,125
Sir, you have so many years of experience.

712
00:36:14,208 --> 00:36:15,541
Let's just go, sir.

713
00:36:16,041 --> 00:36:18,583
So how are we travelling?
Shall we book a train?

714
00:36:18,875 --> 00:36:20,541
No need, can't we just go by bus?

715
00:36:20,583 --> 00:36:22,291
Man, wouldn't that be a huge detour?

716
00:36:22,333 --> 00:36:23,708
We'll have to switch 2-3 buses.

717
00:36:23,750 --> 00:36:25,416
It's fine,
we can enjoy the scenery along the way.

718
00:36:25,458 --> 00:36:26,708
-You want tea, sir?
-Yeah.

719
00:36:26,750 --> 00:36:28,250
-Make it strong.
-Make it two.

720
00:36:29,083 --> 00:36:31,416
PART THREE
RAJU - THE HUSBAND

721
00:36:31,458 --> 00:36:33,708
[mysterious music playing]

722
00:37:22,541 --> 00:37:23,583
Okay.

723
00:37:26,458 --> 00:37:27,500
What did they say, sir?

724
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:29,583
They said
they'll assign two policemen to assist us.

725
00:37:31,125 --> 00:37:32,625
[motorcycle passing]

726
00:37:32,958 --> 00:37:34,875
[mysterious music playing]

727
00:37:44,125 --> 00:37:46,125
[In Kannada]
Was this photo was taken here?

728
00:37:47,250 --> 00:37:48,291
Yes, sir.

729
00:37:48,416 --> 00:37:49,750
Do you know them?

730
00:37:51,166 --> 00:37:53,416
Well... not personally.

731
00:37:54,125 --> 00:37:56,875
They might be from Chitrahalli.

732
00:37:56,916 --> 00:38:00,250
Usually, people from there
come here to take family photos.

733
00:38:01,041 --> 00:38:02,125
What's wrong, sir?

734
00:38:03,666 --> 00:38:05,000
They can't identify them, sir.

735
00:38:05,208 --> 00:38:06,791
They may be from Chitrahalli village.

736
00:38:08,083 --> 00:38:09,750
Ask if he knows this man.

737
00:38:10,958 --> 00:38:12,250
Do you know him?

738
00:38:12,583 --> 00:38:14,875
He's our Kiccha Sudeep, sir.

739
00:38:14,916 --> 00:38:16,375
No, no, no.

740
00:38:16,541 --> 00:38:18,375
I'm asking if you know this man. This guy.

741
00:38:20,333 --> 00:38:21,500
No, sir.

742
00:38:22,541 --> 00:38:23,666
Okay.

743
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:31,291
That village he said,

744
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:32,708
Chitrahalli... how far is it?

745
00:38:32,833 --> 00:38:35,625
It's approximately around
3 kilometres from here.

746
00:38:42,041 --> 00:38:43,750
[song begins]

747
00:38:47,333 --> 00:38:52,083
<i>♪ Beside the emerald fringes
of the paddy fields ♪</i>

748
00:38:52,125 --> 00:38:56,541
<i>♪ Forged in the golden breath
of the midday sun ♪</i>

749
00:39:01,750 --> 00:39:06,250
<i>♪ Beside the emerald fringes
of the paddy fields ♪</i>

750
00:39:06,541 --> 00:39:10,916
<i>♪ Forged in the golden breath
of the midday sun ♪</i>

751
00:39:10,958 --> 00:39:15,708
<i>♪ Walking all alone,
I just can't seem to reach ♪</i>

752
00:39:16,083 --> 00:39:20,500
<i>♪ That little patch of shade
beneath the mango tree ♪</i>

753
00:39:20,916 --> 00:39:25,375
<i>♪ Won't you come and sit by my side? ♪</i>

754
00:39:25,708 --> 00:39:30,166
Let us share a few sweet words

755
00:39:36,833 --> 00:39:38,375
It's quite cold, isn't it, sir?

756
00:39:41,541 --> 00:39:42,708
-Vivek , sir.
-Yes, sir.

757
00:39:44,083 --> 00:39:46,250
Just show that man this photo.

758
00:39:46,375 --> 00:39:47,458
Sir...

759
00:39:47,500 --> 00:39:48,583
Sir... could you give me a light?

760
00:39:48,625 --> 00:39:50,333
Maybe ask the tea maker also.

761
00:39:50,416 --> 00:39:52,583
Do you recognise anyone in this photo?

762
00:39:53,208 --> 00:39:55,166
[mysterious music playing]

763
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:20,125
Do you know this man?

764
00:40:20,166 --> 00:40:21,833
-Sir, they're leaving.
-This is our--

765
00:40:21,875 --> 00:40:23,250
Is it? Give it.

766
00:40:23,666 --> 00:40:24,750
Raju.

767
00:40:39,458 --> 00:40:41,416
My ancestors were from Tamil Nadu, sir.

768
00:40:42,833 --> 00:40:44,500
To make a living,

769
00:40:44,583 --> 00:40:49,333
we moved with our family
to Devanahalli in Karnataka.

770
00:40:50,208 --> 00:40:51,833
Our hereditary trade is

771
00:40:52,125 --> 00:40:53,541
making dolls and toys.

772
00:40:55,083 --> 00:40:58,208
There were many people like us over there.

773
00:40:58,291 --> 00:41:00,041
All of them had come from Tamil Nadu.

774
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:02,625
This was hereditary trade for all of them.

775
00:41:02,666 --> 00:41:06,208
[traffic noise]

776
00:41:07,708 --> 00:41:10,541
I'll go buy two bottles of water.

777
00:41:11,291 --> 00:41:12,958
-Keep an eye on him.
-Okay.

778
00:41:17,125 --> 00:41:19,250
How long has it been
since you married Shobha?

779
00:41:19,541 --> 00:41:20,541
Ten years.

780
00:41:23,458 --> 00:41:24,750
Where did you first meet her?

781
00:41:25,458 --> 00:41:28,208
[melancholic music playing]

782
00:41:31,208 --> 00:41:32,583
A few years ago,

783
00:41:33,125 --> 00:41:35,791
our village was hit by a massive flood.

784
00:41:36,916 --> 00:41:37,916
After that,

785
00:41:38,166 --> 00:41:39,541
a few families like ours

786
00:41:39,916 --> 00:41:41,375
relocated to Bydakotta.

787
00:41:43,791 --> 00:41:47,333
<i>It was on a bus to Bydakotta</i>

788
00:41:48,083 --> 00:41:50,208
<i>when I first saw Shobha. </i>

789
00:41:55,750 --> 00:41:56,833
<i>After that,</i>

790
00:41:56,875 --> 00:41:58,875
<i>we kept running into each other
in our village...</i>

791
00:41:58,916 --> 00:42:03,125
<i>At the temple, the market, and elsewhere.</i>

792
00:42:13,083 --> 00:42:14,291
We got married.

793
00:42:15,625 --> 00:42:17,000
And had two kids.

794
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:32,458
Shobha, is everything ready?

795
00:42:32,791 --> 00:42:33,875
Quick.

796
00:42:34,666 --> 00:42:35,666
Come on.

797
00:42:37,208 --> 00:42:38,875
<i>Due to lack of rains,</i>

798
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:41,958
<i>we couldn't continue our trade
and we were left with nothing.</i>

799
00:42:42,541 --> 00:42:45,583
No one was interested in
buying our dolls, sir.

800
00:42:46,625 --> 00:42:48,166
Our business started falling apart.

801
00:42:48,958 --> 00:42:50,541
We were drowning in poverty.

802
00:42:51,291 --> 00:42:52,708
We didn't know what else to do

803
00:42:52,958 --> 00:42:54,625
so we decided to find another job.

804
00:42:55,250 --> 00:42:58,541
We moved from Bydakotta to Chitrahalli.

805
00:43:01,125 --> 00:43:03,541
That's where I met Ganeshan.

806
00:43:04,500 --> 00:43:05,708
Who's this Ganeshan?

807
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:08,583
He's a distant relative of Shobha's.

808
00:43:09,666 --> 00:43:12,166
He's the one who found us a place to stay.

809
00:43:13,250 --> 00:43:15,708
Ganeshan also got me a job

810
00:43:15,750 --> 00:43:18,291
in films through an art director he knew.

811
00:43:18,416 --> 00:43:20,416
[cargo auto-rickshaw engine rumbling]

812
00:43:23,583 --> 00:43:26,291
[rhythmic music playing]

813
00:43:51,666 --> 00:43:52,875
Want water?

814
00:44:04,041 --> 00:44:05,291
Okay, continue.

815
00:44:06,708 --> 00:44:09,125
I leave for work early in the morning

816
00:44:09,750 --> 00:44:11,250
and return late at night, sir.

817
00:44:13,083 --> 00:44:15,916
I get to see my kids only once a week.

818
00:44:17,541 --> 00:44:19,500
Our happy family

819
00:44:20,666 --> 00:44:22,125
slowly started having small issues

820
00:44:22,208 --> 00:44:24,000
which later turned into big ones.

821
00:44:25,708 --> 00:44:27,375
I have a drinking habit.

822
00:44:27,416 --> 00:44:28,750
I can see that.

823
00:44:30,708 --> 00:44:33,166
Ganeshan was like family to us.

824
00:44:33,958 --> 00:44:36,083
He was very fond of my kids.

825
00:44:37,875 --> 00:44:38,916
Stop here.

826
00:44:42,250 --> 00:44:44,208
-Ride safe.
-You go safe, man.

827
00:44:46,666 --> 00:44:48,291
[chickens clucking]

828
00:44:48,625 --> 00:44:49,916
Behave yourself.

829
00:45:02,583 --> 00:45:03,875
[thudding onto bed]

830
00:45:04,625 --> 00:45:05,791
And then one night,

831
00:45:06,583 --> 00:45:07,583
when I...

832
00:45:09,750 --> 00:45:11,333
got home from work.

833
00:45:13,666 --> 00:45:16,666
[crickets chirping]

834
00:45:57,291 --> 00:45:58,333
<i>Stop it.</i>

835
00:46:04,625 --> 00:46:08,208
[suspenseful music playing]

836
00:46:30,458 --> 00:46:32,416
[melancholic music playing]

837
00:46:35,208 --> 00:46:36,416
Give him some water, sir.

838
00:46:39,250 --> 00:46:40,291
Hey!

839
00:46:40,375 --> 00:46:41,500
Don't cry.

840
00:46:41,708 --> 00:46:42,916
It's okay... Drink up.

841
00:46:52,708 --> 00:46:53,750
I never wanted

842
00:46:53,958 --> 00:46:55,833
to see him in our lives again.

843
00:46:56,291 --> 00:46:58,291
So I decided to move away from him.

844
00:46:58,833 --> 00:47:00,333
My wife, kids, and I

845
00:47:02,083 --> 00:47:03,250
moved to Koduvally.

846
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:31,000
But...

847
00:47:31,625 --> 00:47:33,166
[sobbing]

848
00:47:33,458 --> 00:47:34,500
He...

849
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:37,583
followed us there too, sir.

850
00:47:37,666 --> 00:47:39,708
[train passing]

851
00:47:40,166 --> 00:47:41,541
You said you wanted to go somewhere.

852
00:47:41,583 --> 00:47:42,750
But how can I leave now?

853
00:47:42,791 --> 00:47:44,000
It's getting late.

854
00:47:44,750 --> 00:47:47,625
[mysterious music playing]

855
00:47:57,500 --> 00:47:58,791
I couldn't take...

856
00:47:59,666 --> 00:48:01,416
any more humiliation, sir...

857
00:48:02,250 --> 00:48:03,708
So I took my kids

858
00:48:05,500 --> 00:48:07,166
and came back to my hometown.

859
00:48:12,125 --> 00:48:13,291
Show me...

860
00:48:31,041 --> 00:48:33,291
[wailing]

861
00:48:36,291 --> 00:48:37,333
Sir...

862
00:48:40,625 --> 00:48:42,333
[continuous sobbing]

863
00:48:49,500 --> 00:48:50,958
Sir...

864
00:48:55,041 --> 00:48:56,041
Raju...

865
00:48:59,916 --> 00:49:01,625
Are you sure this is Shobha?

866
00:49:01,958 --> 00:49:03,041
Sir...

867
00:49:03,083 --> 00:49:04,791
This is my Shobha, sir...

868
00:49:04,916 --> 00:49:06,208
-Close it.
-My Shobha...

869
00:49:06,208 --> 00:49:08,500
She left me, sir...

870
00:49:09,250 --> 00:49:10,541
-Let's step outside.
-Sir...

871
00:49:10,791 --> 00:49:12,500
Get up... Let's go out and talk.

872
00:49:14,208 --> 00:49:15,250
Sir...

873
00:49:15,291 --> 00:49:16,541
Come on... Don't cry.

874
00:49:17,333 --> 00:49:18,416
Let's talk outside.

875
00:49:18,541 --> 00:49:19,541
Come...

876
00:49:20,333 --> 00:49:22,416
[melancholic music playing]

877
00:49:23,875 --> 00:49:25,958
Raju, when did you last see Shobha?

878
00:49:26,583 --> 00:49:28,166
The last time I saw her was

879
00:49:28,208 --> 00:49:30,291
when I left for my hometown with my kids.

880
00:49:30,791 --> 00:49:33,375
Do you know why Shobha killed herself?

881
00:49:33,583 --> 00:49:35,250
Must be because of that scoundrel.

882
00:49:35,625 --> 00:49:37,375
He must've abandoned her.

883
00:49:38,583 --> 00:49:39,958
Where are your children?

884
00:49:40,208 --> 00:49:41,583
At my sister's house.

885
00:49:41,875 --> 00:49:43,541
-Where's that?
-Bellooru.

886
00:49:46,500 --> 00:49:48,458
"Since we were living separately

887
00:49:48,708 --> 00:49:51,541
and as I do not wish to take

888
00:49:51,791 --> 00:49:53,333
the body to my hometown,

889
00:49:53,375 --> 00:49:55,666
I request you to
make the necessary arrangements

890
00:49:55,708 --> 00:49:57,166
to cremate the body here itself."

891
00:49:57,583 --> 00:49:59,791
If you've read it and agree, sign here.

892
00:50:00,083 --> 00:50:01,083
Here.

893
00:50:01,125 --> 00:50:03,500
[melancholic music playing]

894
00:50:19,083 --> 00:50:20,083
Alright, sir.

895
00:50:20,791 --> 00:50:21,791
-Bye, sir.
-Alright.

896
00:50:21,875 --> 00:50:22,875
Come.

897
00:50:26,291 --> 00:50:27,416
Sir.

898
00:50:29,291 --> 00:50:30,375
What's happening, Ajeeb?

899
00:50:30,416 --> 00:50:32,500
He has identified the body
as Shobha's, sir.

900
00:50:32,916 --> 00:50:34,541
He doesn't want to take the body home.

901
00:50:34,541 --> 00:50:36,375
He says the kids
shouldn't see her like this.

902
00:50:37,416 --> 00:50:39,708
[soft music playing]

903
00:50:40,250 --> 00:50:42,291
Do you have money to get back?

904
00:50:43,666 --> 00:50:45,875
Are you sure he isn't directly involved?

905
00:50:46,250 --> 00:50:48,375
As of now,
we don't have any evidence against him.

906
00:50:48,958 --> 00:50:50,666
Raju said that when he left with the kids,

907
00:50:50,708 --> 00:50:52,583
that other guy was still with her, right?

908
00:50:53,333 --> 00:50:54,791
-What was his name?
-Ganeshan.

909
00:50:54,833 --> 00:50:56,333
Find out his whereabouts.

910
00:50:56,791 --> 00:50:58,916
We need to know what role he had in this.

911
00:50:59,125 --> 00:51:00,125
Okay, sir.

912
00:51:00,833 --> 00:51:01,875
It's alright, sir.

913
00:51:01,916 --> 00:51:03,083
I can manage.

914
00:51:03,541 --> 00:51:05,250
Sir, I'll somehow make it back.

915
00:51:05,583 --> 00:51:06,583
Keep it.

916
00:51:06,625 --> 00:51:07,750
No need, sir.

917
00:51:08,041 --> 00:51:09,666
-Why, sir?
-Keep it.

918
00:51:09,791 --> 00:51:11,791
Anyway, since the husband
has identified the body,

919
00:51:11,791 --> 00:51:13,375
we can proceed with the burial.

920
00:51:13,666 --> 00:51:15,666
-Did you get his signature on the papers?
-Yes.

921
00:51:15,708 --> 00:51:18,291
Does he have his Aadhaar card
or ration card with him?

922
00:51:20,291 --> 00:51:22,458
What documents would a man
with no address have, right?

923
00:51:22,791 --> 00:51:25,458
Then make the arrangements
at the public crematorium.

924
00:51:25,833 --> 00:51:26,833
Alright, sir.

925
00:51:29,750 --> 00:51:30,791
Raju.

926
00:51:31,125 --> 00:51:33,708
If you get any information about Ganeshan,

927
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:35,166
make sure you let us know.

928
00:51:36,125 --> 00:51:37,125
Okay, sir.

929
00:51:37,250 --> 00:51:38,250
Go on.

930
00:51:42,375 --> 00:51:44,458
[motorcycle passing]

931
00:51:59,166 --> 00:52:01,166
You're listening to Gazals and studying?

932
00:52:01,625 --> 00:52:02,625
Yes.

933
00:52:02,666 --> 00:52:04,666
His songs have a different mood.

934
00:52:05,083 --> 00:52:07,125
Everything I study
gets into my head very fast.

935
00:52:07,208 --> 00:52:08,875
Are all IAS aspirants like this?

936
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:10,333
Yeah, we're all like that.

937
00:52:11,125 --> 00:52:12,125
Walk on.

938
00:52:12,291 --> 00:52:14,083
How come you're back early today?

939
00:52:14,125 --> 00:52:15,750
I just got back from work travel, right?

940
00:52:15,791 --> 00:52:17,333
-Did Uppa's reports come?
-Yeah.

941
00:52:17,375 --> 00:52:20,000
The doctor said there's improvement.

942
00:52:20,208 --> 00:52:21,375
When are your parents coming?

943
00:52:21,416 --> 00:52:23,125
They said they'll stay a few more days

944
00:52:23,166 --> 00:52:24,291
after my sister's delivery.

945
00:52:24,541 --> 00:52:26,166
What will they do here anyway?

946
00:52:26,666 --> 00:52:28,750
Looks like they'll come
only next month now.

947
00:52:29,083 --> 00:52:30,125
I'm just...

948
00:52:30,250 --> 00:52:32,083
going to freshen up and head out.

949
00:52:32,416 --> 00:52:34,125
Got a couple of things to take care of.

950
00:52:34,125 --> 00:52:35,166
Coming?

951
00:52:35,166 --> 00:52:37,583
No... I need to finish my notes.

952
00:52:38,708 --> 00:52:39,750
Okay.

953
00:52:39,750 --> 00:52:40,791
Okay.

954
00:52:41,166 --> 00:52:42,166
Tea?

955
00:52:42,583 --> 00:52:43,708
If you're making, yes.

956
00:52:43,750 --> 00:52:44,750
Then I will.

957
00:52:51,250 --> 00:52:52,625
[door creaking open]

958
00:52:54,500 --> 00:52:56,958
-Hi, sir.
-New probationary SI, right?

959
00:52:56,958 --> 00:52:59,000
-Yes, sir.
-Shivakumar told me about you. Sit.

960
00:53:04,375 --> 00:53:05,791
According to the report,

961
00:53:06,708 --> 00:53:08,791
the cause of death is blockage in the lungs

962
00:53:08,791 --> 00:53:10,666
caused by water and mud from the well.

963
00:53:10,750 --> 00:53:11,958
-Okay.
-But...

964
00:53:12,125 --> 00:53:13,291
for this to be accidental...

965
00:53:13,333 --> 00:53:14,333
I mean...

966
00:53:14,458 --> 00:53:17,083
I don't think she fell into the well
while conscious.

967
00:53:17,833 --> 00:53:18,958
Why makes you say that, sir?

968
00:53:19,208 --> 00:53:20,208
See...

969
00:53:20,291 --> 00:53:22,166
When a person falls into a well,

970
00:53:22,625 --> 00:53:24,208
even if they are pushed,

971
00:53:24,416 --> 00:53:25,666
while they're conscious,

972
00:53:25,708 --> 00:53:27,791
their body instinctively gasps for air.

973
00:53:28,291 --> 00:53:29,125
Okay.

974
00:53:29,166 --> 00:53:30,208
In that situation,

975
00:53:30,333 --> 00:53:31,333
the lungs...

976
00:53:33,250 --> 00:53:36,083
would contain a lot more water.

977
00:53:36,333 --> 00:53:38,958
But here,
the amount of water is quite normal.

978
00:53:38,958 --> 00:53:39,958
-Sir?
-Get the report.

979
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:41,125
Okay, sir.

980
00:53:42,083 --> 00:53:45,375
There's also an injury
on the back of her head.

981
00:53:45,708 --> 00:53:47,041
Maybe she struck her head

982
00:53:47,041 --> 00:53:48,291
while falling into the well.

983
00:53:48,541 --> 00:53:50,000
Or someone may have

984
00:53:50,291 --> 00:53:51,291
hit her from behind.

985
00:53:51,666 --> 00:53:52,791
If that's the case,

986
00:53:52,958 --> 00:53:54,333
someone may have attacked her

987
00:53:54,375 --> 00:53:56,625
before she fell into the well.

988
00:53:58,625 --> 00:54:00,416
Sir, are you suggesting
it could be a murder?

989
00:54:01,166 --> 00:54:02,166
See...

990
00:54:02,166 --> 00:54:04,583
I'm only saying a possibility exists.

991
00:54:05,125 --> 00:54:08,541
The rest is for the police to investigate.

992
00:54:09,458 --> 00:54:11,083
Here's the report.
Everything's in there.

993
00:54:11,083 --> 00:54:13,333
[suspenseful music playing]

994
00:54:34,833 --> 00:54:35,875
Where is Nandakumar , sir?

995
00:54:35,875 --> 00:54:37,500
He's gone on escort for the minister.

996
00:54:40,083 --> 00:54:41,083
You please wait.

997
00:54:41,125 --> 00:54:42,166
Sir will call you in.

998
00:54:44,666 --> 00:54:47,291
<i>The number can't be reached right now.</i>

999
00:55:04,250 --> 00:55:07,000
<i>The number can't be reached right now.</i>

1000
00:55:07,041 --> 00:55:08,916
<i>Please try later.</i>

1001
00:55:11,166 --> 00:55:12,166
Sir.

1002
00:55:13,750 --> 00:55:15,083
Some people are here to see you.

1003
00:55:15,750 --> 00:55:17,083
Please ask them to wait, sir.

1004
00:55:17,250 --> 00:55:18,291
But , sir...

1005
00:55:18,333 --> 00:55:20,666
They said they're the relatives
of the woman

1006
00:55:20,833 --> 00:55:22,458
who was found in the abandoned well.

1007
00:55:22,708 --> 00:55:23,708
Send them in.

1008
00:55:23,750 --> 00:55:24,875
Okay... Come in.

1009
00:55:26,291 --> 00:55:27,291
Go inside.

1010
00:55:28,625 --> 00:55:30,666
-Greetings, sir.
-Greetings, sir.

1011
00:55:31,333 --> 00:55:32,333
Greetings, sir.

1012
00:55:32,666 --> 00:55:33,666
What is this regarding?

1013
00:55:33,791 --> 00:55:35,291
Sir, my name is Nanjappa.

1014
00:55:35,458 --> 00:55:37,750
We read in the newspaper that Raju,

1015
00:55:37,791 --> 00:55:40,666
Shobha's husband, had come here.

1016
00:55:41,291 --> 00:55:43,125
Yes. Raju came here earlier.

1017
00:55:43,250 --> 00:55:45,666
Sir, this is Raju's mother.

1018
00:55:48,583 --> 00:55:49,916
This is his sister.

1019
00:55:50,041 --> 00:55:51,208
And this is my brother.

1020
00:55:51,666 --> 00:55:52,708
Mister...

1021
00:55:52,875 --> 00:55:54,625
We've already cremated the body.

1022
00:55:54,791 --> 00:55:56,291
That's not why we are here, sir.

1023
00:55:56,333 --> 00:55:58,333
We haven't heard from Raju in over a year.

1024
00:55:58,625 --> 00:55:59,625
No matter where he is,

1025
00:55:59,666 --> 00:56:01,708
he'd return to the village
at least twice a year.

1026
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:03,291
He'd come see his mother,

1027
00:56:03,333 --> 00:56:04,916
attend the temple festival and leave.

1028
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:06,708
But it's been over a year

1029
00:56:06,750 --> 00:56:08,291
since he last came home.

1030
00:56:08,291 --> 00:56:09,541
How can that be?

1031
00:56:09,541 --> 00:56:11,416
But didn't Raju come by three months ago

1032
00:56:11,458 --> 00:56:13,083
to leave his children at your house?

1033
00:56:13,208 --> 00:56:14,208
No, sir.

1034
00:56:14,375 --> 00:56:16,958
I last saw his children over a year ago.

1035
00:56:17,791 --> 00:56:20,166
Does Raju have any siblings besides you?

1036
00:56:20,208 --> 00:56:21,208
No, sir.

1037
00:56:23,500 --> 00:56:25,250
You live in Bellooru, right?

1038
00:56:25,666 --> 00:56:27,000
No, sir. Chitrahalli.

1039
00:56:27,250 --> 00:56:29,000
Bellooru is a forest area, sir.

1040
00:56:29,333 --> 00:56:32,083
We weren't lying when we said Raju came.

1041
00:56:32,875 --> 00:56:33,916
Look.

1042
00:56:33,916 --> 00:56:36,541
[mysterious music playing]

1043
00:56:41,500 --> 00:56:42,541
What's it?

1044
00:56:42,708 --> 00:56:44,166
That's not Raju, sir.

1045
00:56:46,458 --> 00:56:47,541
Then?

1046
00:56:47,583 --> 00:56:48,666
This is Bhuvanesh.

1047
00:56:48,666 --> 00:56:50,458
A distant relative of Shobha's.

1048
00:56:57,041 --> 00:56:58,916
Isn't this Shobha with her children?

1049
00:57:00,541 --> 00:57:02,166
And isn't that Raju standing beside her?

1050
00:57:02,458 --> 00:57:04,125
That's Shobha and her children.

1051
00:57:04,250 --> 00:57:07,000
But the man standing with them isn't Raju.
It's Bhuvanesh.

1052
00:57:07,958 --> 00:57:09,958
How dare you come to a police station
and lie?

1053
00:57:10,083 --> 00:57:12,375
No, sir. We're telling the truth.

1054
00:57:17,583 --> 00:57:18,791
Bloody fools!

1055
00:57:19,083 --> 00:57:21,208
What exactly are you people doing
as police officers?

1056
00:57:21,250 --> 00:57:22,250
Huh?

1057
00:57:22,375 --> 00:57:23,833
This is no longer a 174 case.

1058
00:57:23,875 --> 00:57:24,875
This is murder.

1059
00:57:24,958 --> 00:57:26,458
A possible suspect

1060
00:57:26,708 --> 00:57:28,375
came here crying and put on an act,

1061
00:57:28,375 --> 00:57:29,583
and you let him walk out

1062
00:57:29,625 --> 00:57:31,333
without even checking his background?

1063
00:57:31,500 --> 00:57:33,750
Don't just stand there staring at me.

1064
00:57:34,416 --> 00:57:35,625
I specifically told you

1065
00:57:35,666 --> 00:57:37,708
to keep a close watch on these two.

1066
00:57:37,958 --> 00:57:40,416
But , sir, we had no evidence against him.

1067
00:57:40,416 --> 00:57:41,750
Of course you didn't.

1068
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:43,958
You expect the evidence
come looking for you?

1069
00:57:43,958 --> 00:57:46,583
You can explain all this
to your seniors once you're suspended.

1070
00:57:47,500 --> 00:57:49,250
How many years of service do you have?

1071
00:57:49,958 --> 00:57:51,166
Twenty-four.

1072
00:57:51,166 --> 00:57:52,500
Hmph... Twenty-four!

1073
00:57:52,625 --> 00:57:53,875
For what?

1074
00:57:55,708 --> 00:57:57,333
Hope you haven't forgotten your old job.

1075
00:57:57,375 --> 00:57:59,416
-No, sir.
-Well get it dusted.

1076
00:57:59,708 --> 00:58:02,291
At this rate, you'll lose your cap
before your probation ends

1077
00:58:03,958 --> 00:58:05,750
I'm giving you 24 hours.

1078
00:58:05,833 --> 00:58:07,833
If the suspect isn't
in front of me by then,

1079
00:58:07,833 --> 00:58:09,500
I'll make sure all of you suffer for it.

1080
00:58:09,541 --> 00:58:10,541
I'm serious.

1081
00:58:10,875 --> 00:58:11,916
You may go.

1082
00:58:15,708 --> 00:58:19,791
[temple devotional song playing]

1083
00:58:21,500 --> 00:58:23,416
[stage performance percussion]

1084
00:59:23,791 --> 00:59:25,208
Hey, you!

1085
00:59:25,541 --> 00:59:27,250
[rhythm intensifies]

1086
00:59:27,375 --> 00:59:28,708
Stop right there!

1087
01:00:19,875 --> 01:00:21,041
[thudding to the ground]

1088
01:00:34,041 --> 01:00:35,666
[scuffling]

1089
01:01:03,291 --> 01:01:05,833
[heavy thud]

1090
01:01:29,416 --> 01:01:30,541
So...

1091
01:01:30,708 --> 01:01:31,833
Shall we take him?

1092
01:01:31,958 --> 01:01:34,000
[suspenseful music playing]

1093
01:01:40,958 --> 01:01:42,083
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

1094
01:01:42,916 --> 01:01:44,125
<i>I am not Raju.</i>

1095
01:01:44,416 --> 01:01:45,541
<i>I am Bhuvanesh.</i>

1096
01:01:46,208 --> 01:01:50,458
PART FOUR
RAJU/ BHUVANESH - THE ACCUSED

1097
01:01:52,750 --> 01:01:54,875
Shobha is my distant relative.

1098
01:01:55,916 --> 01:01:57,125
From a young age,

1099
01:01:57,833 --> 01:01:58,958
Shobha and I...

1100
01:01:59,166 --> 01:02:01,125
were in love with each other.

1101
01:02:01,875 --> 01:02:02,875
But...

1102
01:02:03,208 --> 01:02:04,500
her family was against it.

1103
01:02:05,000 --> 01:02:08,416
So they got her married to Raju.

1104
01:02:09,458 --> 01:02:10,458
One day,

1105
01:02:11,208 --> 01:02:13,625
I received a letter from Shobha's mother.

1106
01:02:14,333 --> 01:02:15,625
Raju didn't have a job,

1107
01:02:16,416 --> 01:02:18,000
and they were struggling badly.

1108
01:02:18,583 --> 01:02:19,583
So,

1109
01:02:20,083 --> 01:02:21,708
I asked Raju and Shobha

1110
01:02:21,958 --> 01:02:23,166
to come to Chitrahalli.

1111
01:02:23,375 --> 01:02:24,500
Hey!

1112
01:02:24,750 --> 01:02:26,166
Look at me, will you?

1113
01:02:28,250 --> 01:02:29,458
You're not alone any more.

1114
01:02:30,250 --> 01:02:31,625
You have a wife and two children.

1115
01:02:31,875 --> 01:02:33,500
And all you do is get drunk.

1116
01:02:33,708 --> 01:02:34,916
If you go on like this...

1117
01:02:35,041 --> 01:02:36,208
like some lunatic...

1118
01:02:38,916 --> 01:02:41,333
Keep behaving like a madman,
you'll only ruin everything.

1119
01:02:41,541 --> 01:02:42,666
I'm warning you!

1120
01:02:47,041 --> 01:02:49,750
Meenu, come. Want something to eat?

1121
01:02:51,000 --> 01:02:52,666
[melodious music playing]

1122
01:02:52,875 --> 01:02:53,875
Here you go.

1123
01:02:56,291 --> 01:02:57,458
Do you like it?

1124
01:02:58,291 --> 01:03:00,375
[auto-rickshaw engine rumbling]

1125
01:03:14,500 --> 01:03:15,541
What's it?

1126
01:03:16,000 --> 01:03:17,500
This is the mansion you'll be living in.

1127
01:03:17,541 --> 01:03:18,541
Is it good?

1128
01:03:50,500 --> 01:03:51,541
Meenu...

1129
01:03:51,541 --> 01:03:52,750
Did you like it?

1130
01:04:14,875 --> 01:04:16,541
Hey, watch out! Careful!

1131
01:04:17,166 --> 01:04:19,666
How many times have I told you
not to drink in broad daylight?

1132
01:04:20,291 --> 01:04:21,416
Why are you like this?

1133
01:04:21,458 --> 01:04:23,541
Do you even realise
the trouble you're causing?

1134
01:04:26,375 --> 01:04:27,500
Hey...

1135
01:04:28,166 --> 01:04:29,708
There... Easy... Careful...

1136
01:04:30,416 --> 01:04:31,666
Lie down... Come on...

1137
01:04:33,208 --> 01:04:34,458
This isn't right.

1138
01:04:39,875 --> 01:04:41,500
[soft music playing]

1139
01:04:56,375 --> 01:04:58,250
[song begins]

1140
01:05:15,458 --> 01:05:19,916
<i>♪ To test the pure gold of my love ♪</i>

1141
01:05:20,291 --> 01:05:24,541
<i>♪ Your heart became the truest touchstone ♪</i>

1142
01:05:25,041 --> 01:05:29,500
<i>♪ To test the pure gold of my love ♪</i>

1143
01:05:29,833 --> 01:05:34,208
<i>♪ Your heart became the truest touchstone ♪</i>

1144
01:05:34,708 --> 01:05:38,958
<i>♪ Seeking to weave a haven of our own ♪</i>

1145
01:05:39,416 --> 01:05:44,458
<i>♪ You were a resting branch
of silver moonbeams ♪</i>

1146
01:05:46,708 --> 01:05:51,166
<i>♪ Here, in the southern courtyard
fragrant with wild jasmine ♪</i>

1147
01:05:51,458 --> 01:05:55,750
<i>♪ An eternity, it seems,
I have waited for you ♪</i>

1148
01:05:56,250 --> 01:06:00,708
<i>♪ Here, in the southern courtyard
fragrant with wild jasmine ♪</i>

1149
01:06:01,083 --> 01:06:05,375
<i>♪ An eternity, it seems,
I have waited for you ♪</i>

1150
01:06:10,666 --> 01:06:15,083
<i>♪ Forged in the golden breath
of the midday sun ♪</i>

1151
01:06:15,416 --> 01:06:19,791
<i>♪ Beside the emerald fringes
of the paddy fields ♪</i>

1152
01:06:20,333 --> 01:06:24,708
<i>♪ Forged in the golden breath
of the midday sun ♪</i>

1153
01:06:25,125 --> 01:06:29,375
<i>♪ Beside the emerald fringes
of the paddy fields ♪</i>

1154
01:06:29,541 --> 01:06:34,208
<i>♪ Walking all alone,
I just can't seem to reach ♪</i>

1155
01:06:34,250 --> 01:06:35,250
Why did you buy so much?

1156
01:06:35,250 --> 01:06:37,416
<i>♪ Beneath the mango tree's fragile
quilt of shade ♪</i>

1157
01:06:37,416 --> 01:06:38,791
Hey, careful. Can you manage it?

1158
01:06:38,833 --> 01:06:40,250
You think this is too heavy for me?

1159
01:06:40,416 --> 01:06:43,875
<i>♪ Come, linger by my side awhile ♪</i>

1160
01:06:44,291 --> 01:06:48,583
<i>♪ Let us trade a handful of tender truths ♪</i>

1161
01:06:49,166 --> 01:06:53,458
<i>♪ Come, linger by my side awhile ♪</i>

1162
01:06:53,916 --> 01:06:56,625
<i>♪ Let us trade a handful of tender truths ♪</i>

1163
01:06:56,666 --> 01:06:58,000
What's it?

1164
01:07:00,208 --> 01:07:01,958
See what I've bought for you!

1165
01:07:18,208 --> 01:07:19,208
Did you like it?

1166
01:07:22,750 --> 01:07:23,958
You know...

1167
01:07:24,166 --> 01:07:26,000
All famous actresses use this.

1168
01:07:29,125 --> 01:07:30,541
Seems expensive.

1169
01:07:32,208 --> 01:07:33,791
Why are you looking at me like that?

1170
01:07:34,041 --> 01:07:35,166
Should I not?

1171
01:07:39,708 --> 01:07:41,083
Can't I look at you?

1172
01:07:44,208 --> 01:07:45,250
Tell me...

1173
01:07:55,833 --> 01:07:58,333
[goats bleating]

1174
01:08:03,541 --> 01:08:05,666
[suspenseful music playing]

1175
01:09:16,833 --> 01:09:17,916
What happened?

1176
01:09:17,958 --> 01:09:19,291
Seems like someone was here.

1177
01:09:26,916 --> 01:09:28,125
<i>After that,</i>

1178
01:09:28,208 --> 01:09:29,333
<i>Raju was...</i>

1179
01:09:30,208 --> 01:09:31,375
<i>never seen again.</i>

1180
01:09:31,875 --> 01:09:33,041
No one knows

1181
01:09:33,333 --> 01:09:34,541
the real reason

1182
01:09:35,333 --> 01:09:36,500
why he

1183
01:09:37,333 --> 01:09:39,083
left home like that.

1184
01:09:39,166 --> 01:09:40,291
Until today.

1185
01:09:44,041 --> 01:09:45,041
After that,

1186
01:09:46,250 --> 01:09:47,458
Shobha and I

1187
01:09:48,041 --> 01:09:49,750
left without telling anyone

1188
01:09:50,541 --> 01:09:51,708
and moved to Koduvally, sir.

1189
01:09:51,708 --> 01:09:53,791
[train passing]

1190
01:10:07,583 --> 01:10:08,625
Deva...

1191
01:10:09,208 --> 01:10:10,375
Eat before you go.

1192
01:10:10,958 --> 01:10:12,208
I don't want.

1193
01:10:12,625 --> 01:10:13,666
Deva...

1194
01:10:16,000 --> 01:10:18,458
I asked you to eat.
But you won't listen.

1195
01:10:20,958 --> 01:10:22,750
Don't come here. Move.

1196
01:10:22,791 --> 01:10:24,500
Clear off! Move!

1197
01:10:24,541 --> 01:10:25,458
[camera shutter clicking]

1198
01:10:25,458 --> 01:10:26,708
Move.

1199
01:10:26,833 --> 01:10:27,916
Sir.

1200
01:10:28,041 --> 01:10:29,166
IP is on the line, sir.

1201
01:10:29,833 --> 01:10:32,333
Why did you choose to settle in Koduvally?

1202
01:10:33,250 --> 01:10:34,541
To ruin our peace.

1203
01:10:34,625 --> 01:10:35,625
What else?

1204
01:10:36,333 --> 01:10:37,666
I had come here

1205
01:10:38,000 --> 01:10:39,291
for a shoot years ago.

1206
01:10:39,583 --> 01:10:40,583
I see.

1207
01:10:41,166 --> 01:10:43,208
Then why did you change your name to Raju?

1208
01:10:43,500 --> 01:10:44,833
Shobha asked me to.

1209
01:10:45,458 --> 01:10:46,500
She said only then

1210
01:10:46,541 --> 01:10:47,916
people here would believe

1211
01:10:47,916 --> 01:10:49,500
we're husband and wife.

1212
01:10:52,083 --> 01:10:55,125
So you said the two of you
were living happily here.

1213
01:10:55,916 --> 01:10:57,833
Then how did it end in murder?

1214
01:10:59,541 --> 01:11:02,333
[crowd clamoring]

1215
01:11:11,250 --> 01:11:12,875
You said you'd be back only tomorrow.

1216
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:14,000
Rain.

1217
01:11:14,000 --> 01:11:15,208
The shoot got called off.

1218
01:11:15,416 --> 01:11:17,041
It'll resume only after the rain clears.

1219
01:11:17,041 --> 01:11:18,041
Is that so?

1220
01:11:18,083 --> 01:11:19,333
Here, give these to the kids.

1221
01:11:19,916 --> 01:11:21,875
I'm starving. Serve the food.

1222
01:11:30,125 --> 01:11:31,125
Meenu.

1223
01:11:31,583 --> 01:11:32,583
Meenu, my dear...

1224
01:11:32,750 --> 01:11:34,583
See what I've brought for you.

1225
01:11:35,625 --> 01:11:36,875
Where are the kids?

1226
01:11:39,041 --> 01:11:40,458
Hey, I'm asking where the kids are.

1227
01:11:40,958 --> 01:11:41,958
Food...

1228
01:11:42,500 --> 01:11:43,625
is ready.

1229
01:11:44,333 --> 01:11:45,500
-Come and eat--
-Hey!

1230
01:11:46,791 --> 01:11:48,125
I'm asking about the kids

1231
01:11:48,125 --> 01:11:49,708
and you're talking about food?

1232
01:11:50,791 --> 01:11:52,208
Where are they?

1233
01:11:52,958 --> 01:11:54,333
Why are you shouting so much?

1234
01:11:54,583 --> 01:11:55,583
As if...

1235
01:11:55,666 --> 01:11:56,833
they're your own children.

1236
01:11:57,250 --> 01:11:59,541
They may not be mine by blood,

1237
01:11:59,583 --> 01:12:01,416
but I've raised them like my own.

1238
01:12:01,791 --> 01:12:02,791
So what?

1239
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:04,000
So what?!

1240
01:12:04,833 --> 01:12:06,916
Tell me where the kids are!

1241
01:12:07,541 --> 01:12:08,541
Tell me the truth.

1242
01:12:09,750 --> 01:12:10,958
What did you do to them?

1243
01:12:11,791 --> 01:12:13,958
Their father came and took them away.

1244
01:12:14,166 --> 01:12:15,208
Their father?!

1245
01:12:15,708 --> 01:12:16,791
Which father?

1246
01:12:16,833 --> 01:12:18,500
Why does it bother you if they're gone?

1247
01:12:20,791 --> 01:12:22,083
I'm still here, aren't I?

1248
01:12:23,833 --> 01:12:25,500
Maybe it's better they left.

1249
01:12:26,125 --> 01:12:28,166
They were nothing but an extra burden.

1250
01:12:28,625 --> 01:12:29,791
Extra burden?

1251
01:12:29,958 --> 01:12:30,833
[slapping]

1252
01:12:30,833 --> 01:12:32,000
[head thudding]

1253
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:34,583
I never thought you'd sink this low.

1254
01:12:34,791 --> 01:12:36,375
You called your own children a burden.

1255
01:12:36,375 --> 01:12:38,125
I can't stay with you another second...

1256
01:12:44,666 --> 01:12:45,666
Shobha...

1257
01:12:45,833 --> 01:12:47,625
[mysterious music playing]

1258
01:12:48,041 --> 01:12:49,041
Hey...

1259
01:12:58,041 --> 01:12:59,041
Shobha...

1260
01:13:11,916 --> 01:13:14,416
[suspenseful music playing]

1261
01:13:30,625 --> 01:13:32,458
[owl hooting]

1262
01:13:54,125 --> 01:13:56,708
[festival percussion playing]

1263
01:14:44,916 --> 01:14:46,458
[mysterious music playing]

1264
01:14:46,500 --> 01:14:49,458
<i>Under Section 167 of the CrPC,</i>

1265
01:14:50,041 --> 01:14:55,000
<i>this court remands the accused,
Bhuvanesh Kumar alias Bhuvanesh,</i>

1266
01:14:55,041 --> 01:14:57,666
<i>to fourteen days of judicial custody.</i>

1267
01:14:57,708 --> 01:14:59,000
SHOBHA MURDER CASE

1268
01:14:59,041 --> 01:15:00,750
In a way, it's good he confessed himself.

1269
01:15:00,791 --> 01:15:02,791
Otherwise it would've been
a real headache for us.

1270
01:15:02,791 --> 01:15:03,833
True, sir.

1271
01:15:04,541 --> 01:15:06,666
But Raju and the kids
are still missing, sir.

1272
01:15:06,875 --> 01:15:08,666
He said Raju took the children, right?

1273
01:15:09,166 --> 01:15:11,541
And they didn't disappear
within our station limits.

1274
01:15:11,583 --> 01:15:13,166
There's no written complaint either.

1275
01:15:13,166 --> 01:15:15,333
Sir, we only know what Bhuvanesh told us.

1276
01:15:15,458 --> 01:15:16,750
Let a complaint come first.

1277
01:15:16,791 --> 01:15:17,791
We'll deal with it then.

1278
01:15:17,791 --> 01:15:19,833
Why invite unnecessary trouble?

1279
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:21,041
Okay, sir.

1280
01:15:21,041 --> 01:15:22,041
Alright then.

1281
01:15:32,750 --> 01:15:34,291
Sometimes when we crack a case,

1282
01:15:34,791 --> 01:15:38,458
it feels great
hearing seniors appreciate us.

1283
01:15:39,333 --> 01:15:41,625
But if things go the other way,

1284
01:15:41,875 --> 01:15:44,458
the things that come out
of their mouths then...

1285
01:15:44,583 --> 01:15:46,333
your eardrums will burst hearing them.

1286
01:15:51,666 --> 01:15:53,500
What are you thinking about, sir?

1287
01:15:54,000 --> 01:15:55,000
I was just...

1288
01:15:55,458 --> 01:15:57,250
thinking about Raju and the children.

1289
01:15:57,916 --> 01:15:59,666
Sir, you're still stuck on that?

1290
01:15:59,958 --> 01:16:01,708
I don't mean to advise you, but...

1291
01:16:02,083 --> 01:16:04,291
Just because you're new and full of fire,

1292
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,916
don't dig too deep into everything.

1293
01:16:07,250 --> 01:16:09,291
It'll become a huge headache later.

1294
01:16:09,875 --> 01:16:13,541
No point acting more righteous
than our bloody seniors.

1295
01:16:13,583 --> 01:16:14,625
Joy... stop it.

1296
01:16:15,000 --> 01:16:16,041
Oh, sorry.

1297
01:16:16,083 --> 01:16:17,916
You're in full swing today, Joy , sir.

1298
01:16:18,083 --> 01:16:19,375
No, nothing like that.

1299
01:16:19,416 --> 01:16:20,500
Enough, Joy.

1300
01:16:20,541 --> 01:16:22,291
I've been counting.
You've crossed the limit.

1301
01:16:22,333 --> 01:16:23,416
Limit?

1302
01:16:23,750 --> 01:16:25,625
Today's Ajeeb , sir's treat.

1303
01:16:25,625 --> 01:16:27,416
-You hear that?
-Oh, is it now?

1304
01:16:28,708 --> 01:16:30,583
[jeep passing]

1305
01:16:36,208 --> 01:16:38,333
Hello, this is Dharmadom Police Station.

1306
01:16:38,750 --> 01:16:40,083
Whom you want? Goa?

1307
01:16:40,708 --> 01:16:42,375
Yes... Yes, sir.

1308
01:16:42,708 --> 01:16:44,625
No cases register here.

1309
01:16:44,666 --> 01:16:45,791
Madhu , sir...

1310
01:16:45,875 --> 01:16:47,708
-Sir... It's in English.
-You're sweating.

1311
01:16:48,166 --> 01:16:49,958
Hello, this is the station SI speaking.

1312
01:16:50,916 --> 01:16:52,583
Yeah, just give me the case details.

1313
01:16:56,708 --> 01:16:58,250
The address also, please?

1314
01:17:02,291 --> 01:17:03,333
Okay.

1315
01:17:05,208 --> 01:17:06,250
Okay.

1316
01:17:06,291 --> 01:17:07,291
We'll go to the address.

1317
01:17:07,333 --> 01:17:09,333
If there's somebody there,
we'll call you back.

1318
01:17:11,208 --> 01:17:14,291
Go to this address
and bring those people to the station.

1319
01:17:14,333 --> 01:17:15,250
Okay, sir.

1320
01:17:15,291 --> 01:17:17,541
And on the way back,
find yourself a good English tutor.

1321
01:17:17,583 --> 01:17:19,625
Good thing you were there
this time too, sir.

1322
01:17:19,833 --> 01:17:22,375
Last time it was Hindi from Karnataka.

1323
01:17:22,500 --> 01:17:24,500
Now it's English from Goa.

1324
01:17:24,625 --> 01:17:26,041
Wonder who's going to call next.

1325
01:17:33,333 --> 01:17:34,958
No more calls!

1326
01:17:35,416 --> 01:17:37,958
<i>Last time it was Hindi from Karnataka.</i>

1327
01:17:38,083 --> 01:17:40,458
<i>Now it's English from Goa.</i>

1328
01:17:40,500 --> 01:17:43,416
