1833
01:54:51,166 --> 01:54:54,208
An inspector from Dharavi station,
Keerti Deshpande.

1834
01:54:54,416 --> 01:54:57,666
I had sent the kids' photos and details
to several people.

1835
01:54:58,250 --> 01:54:59,916
She said two kids matching the description

1836
01:54:59,958 --> 01:55:01,583
were brought to a shelter in Dharavi.

1837
01:55:02,583 --> 01:55:06,375
There's a group there that provides shelter
to such orphan kids.

1838
01:55:06,916 --> 01:55:09,625
But she said it's dangerous
to keep them there for too long.

1839
01:55:10,083 --> 01:55:12,291
Are they sure they are the same kids
we're looking for?

1840
01:55:12,375 --> 01:55:14,458
Well, she doesn't have a photo to confirm.

1841
01:55:14,625 --> 01:55:17,333
She wants us to go there, confirm
and bring them back.

1842
01:55:17,958 --> 01:55:19,875
So what do we do? Shall we go?

1843
01:55:21,250 --> 01:55:23,208
I don't have much hope, Joy , sir.

1844
01:55:23,916 --> 01:55:25,666
Besides, I'm tired of running after this.

1845
01:55:27,250 --> 01:55:28,375
I'm done.

1846
01:55:28,458 --> 01:55:29,666
Ajeeb , sir,

1847
01:55:29,833 --> 01:55:33,000
why don't we make one last attempt?

1848
01:55:34,750 --> 01:55:36,791
This time, I'll come with you too.

1849
01:55:36,833 --> 01:55:38,708
[suspenseful music playing]

1850
01:55:42,000 --> 01:55:44,583
If by any chance they are those kids,

1851
01:55:45,291 --> 01:55:48,250
we will regret it
for the rest of our lives.

1852
01:55:49,333 --> 01:55:50,458
That...

1853
01:55:51,041 --> 01:55:52,750
I won't be able to bear, Ajeeb sir.

1854
01:55:53,625 --> 01:55:56,625
[melancholic music playing]

1855
01:56:31,875 --> 01:56:32,958
I'll be leaving now.

1856
01:56:36,583 --> 01:56:37,875
[traffic noise]

1857
01:56:37,875 --> 01:56:40,166
[loud humming]

1858
01:56:42,000 --> 01:56:45,000
[vehicles honking]

1859
01:56:47,083 --> 01:56:49,541
You saw the situation here, didn't you?

1860
01:56:49,625 --> 01:56:51,875
Seriously, you should have come
two days ago.

1861
01:56:51,875 --> 01:56:54,625
We've informed the DCP about this.

1862
01:56:55,041 --> 01:56:56,625
Madam will be here soon.

1863
01:56:56,916 --> 01:56:58,750
She will speak to both of you.

1864
01:56:58,750 --> 01:56:59,750
Alright, sir.

1865
01:56:59,791 --> 01:57:01,333
Let's see what can be done after that.

1866
01:57:01,500 --> 01:57:03,375
When will madam arrive?

1867
01:57:05,208 --> 01:57:06,208
Jai Hind, madam.

1868
01:57:08,750 --> 01:57:09,958
-Ajeeb Rahman?
-Yes, ma'am.

1869
01:57:10,000 --> 01:57:11,000
Come inside.

1870
01:57:11,166 --> 01:57:12,916
-Bring that file inside.
-Okay, madam.

1871
01:57:13,333 --> 01:57:14,458
She's asking us to come inside.

1872
01:57:14,500 --> 01:57:15,541
Thank you, sir.

1873
01:57:17,500 --> 01:57:18,583
Have a seat.

1874
01:57:20,208 --> 01:57:21,375
Tea or coffee?

1875
01:57:21,416 --> 01:57:22,500
No, ma'am. Thank you.

1876
01:57:22,875 --> 01:57:23,875
[bell ringing]

1877
01:57:23,916 --> 01:57:24,958
Madam?

1878
01:57:25,000 --> 01:57:26,791
-Bring three cups of tea.
-Right away, madam.

1879
01:57:29,375 --> 01:57:30,416
So, tell me.

1880
01:57:31,458 --> 01:57:33,125
What's your connection with these children?

1881
01:57:33,583 --> 01:57:37,125
Ma'am, their mother was murdered
in our station limits.

1882
01:57:37,208 --> 01:57:40,041
And... the children have been missing
since then.

1883
01:57:40,333 --> 01:57:43,208
Are you here on official duty?

1884
01:57:44,666 --> 01:57:46,875
Not exactly, ma'am.

1885
01:57:47,375 --> 01:57:49,708
But we believe it is part of our duty too.

1886
01:57:50,625 --> 01:57:52,500
We couldn't stop thinking about
those children, ma'am.

1887
01:57:52,541 --> 01:57:53,916
-Madam.
-Give it to me.

1888
01:57:57,958 --> 01:57:59,250
The thing is,

1889
01:58:00,125 --> 01:58:02,833
these kids are currently in a shelter
near Dharavi.

1890
01:58:02,875 --> 01:58:03,750
Okay.

1891
01:58:03,791 --> 01:58:06,958
Some railway cleaner caught these kids
and sold them to goons.

1892
01:58:07,166 --> 01:58:09,375
That scumbag probably got a cut too.

1893
01:58:10,250 --> 01:58:11,500
The problem is,

1894
01:58:11,541 --> 01:58:14,041
the people running this shelter are
very dangerous.

1895
01:58:14,125 --> 01:58:15,625
They are highly connected.

1896
01:58:16,458 --> 01:58:18,750
We don't know
which bidder they were sold to.

1897
01:58:21,458 --> 01:58:24,125
When I called you that day,
why didn't you all come right away?

1898
01:58:25,333 --> 01:58:27,166
I didn't understand anything!

1899
01:58:28,750 --> 01:58:30,500
She is saying we're late.

1900
01:58:31,583 --> 01:58:33,750
They may have sold the kids
to someone it seems.

1901
01:58:36,291 --> 01:58:38,708
Ma'am, it's very important that
we find these children.

1902
01:58:40,083 --> 01:58:42,625
It won't be easy for us
without your help.

1903
01:58:43,291 --> 01:58:44,500
I understand, Ajeeb.

1904
01:58:45,250 --> 01:58:47,458
If those kids are in that shelter,

1905
01:58:47,500 --> 01:58:49,875
I will do everything I can, in my capacity.

1906
01:58:49,916 --> 01:58:50,833
Okay?

1907
01:58:50,875 --> 01:58:51,666
Okay.

1908
01:58:51,708 --> 01:58:53,333
I'll put my best man on it.

1909
01:58:53,500 --> 01:58:55,875
[phone ringing]

1910
01:58:56,083 --> 01:58:57,708
-It's from our station.
-Okay.

1911
01:59:03,375 --> 01:59:04,708
Ma'am, can I ask you something?

1912
01:59:05,000 --> 01:59:06,041
Go ahead.

1913
01:59:06,291 --> 01:59:09,250
Since you know all of this is happening
right under your nose,

1914
01:59:09,458 --> 01:59:11,291
why haven't you done anything
to stop them?

1915
01:59:17,583 --> 01:59:18,625
Ajeeb...

1916
01:59:18,625 --> 01:59:21,541
After joining the force,
I soon realised something.

1917
01:59:22,041 --> 01:59:23,791
Being hasty doesn't help.

1918
01:59:23,833 --> 01:59:24,833
Okay.

1919
01:59:25,250 --> 01:59:27,083
Balance is very important.

1920
01:59:28,250 --> 01:59:29,958
If you want to change the system,

1921
01:59:29,958 --> 01:59:31,958
you have to work from within it.

1922
01:59:33,375 --> 01:59:34,750
If you don't,

1923
01:59:34,791 --> 01:59:36,791
you'll just end up with
suspensions and transfers.

1924
01:59:37,708 --> 01:59:38,750
Have it.

1925
01:59:44,083 --> 01:59:45,958
There are a lot of cockroaches
in this world.

1926
01:59:46,625 --> 01:59:48,333
You can't eliminate them completely.

1927
01:59:48,666 --> 01:59:50,166
But you can draw a line,

1928
01:59:50,166 --> 01:59:52,041
and that's what I did
within my jurisdiction.

1929
01:59:52,500 --> 01:59:54,500
I didn't let them cross over.

1930
01:59:56,250 --> 01:59:57,791
But to achieve that, sometimes...

1931
01:59:57,833 --> 02:00:00,833
You have to work
with your eyes and ears closed.

1932
02:00:01,125 --> 02:00:03,458
So that, in the bigger picture
everything is alright.

1933
02:00:03,708 --> 02:00:06,750
Ajeeb, it feels nice to know
there are officers like yourself

1934
02:00:07,041 --> 02:00:09,000
who uphold humanity in the force.

1935
02:00:11,000 --> 02:00:12,375
This is SI Pednekar.

1936
02:00:15,375 --> 02:00:16,750
-Hello.
-Hi.

1937
02:00:16,958 --> 02:00:18,125
He will join you.

1938
02:00:18,166 --> 02:00:19,500
Thank you for all your help, ma'am.

1939
02:00:19,583 --> 02:00:21,083
-Good luck.
-Thank you.

1940
02:00:21,500 --> 02:00:22,666
Glad we got to meet you.

1941
02:00:22,875 --> 02:00:24,708
[upbeat music playing]

1942
02:00:26,791 --> 02:00:29,333
[music swells]

1943
02:00:39,916 --> 02:00:41,333
-Park here. We'll be right back.
-Okay, sir.

1944
02:00:41,375 --> 02:00:42,791
-Just park in front.
-Okay, sir.

1945
02:00:43,833 --> 02:00:45,583
-Is this the place?
-Yes. This is the area.

1946
02:00:45,791 --> 02:00:46,958
We need to go a bit further.

1947
02:00:47,000 --> 02:00:48,125
Come. I'll show you.

1948
02:00:48,166 --> 02:00:49,500
It's a slightly sensitive area.

1949
02:00:49,541 --> 02:00:50,541
This is...

1950
02:00:50,625 --> 02:00:51,958
Mumbai's Dharavi.

1951
02:01:46,125 --> 02:01:48,250
[upbeat music playing]

1952
02:01:59,708 --> 02:02:01,041
Hey, is Salim upstairs?

1953
02:02:01,166 --> 02:02:02,208
Yes, he's having food.

1954
02:02:09,791 --> 02:02:11,708
[audio from tv]

1955
02:02:19,291 --> 02:02:20,708
Idiot, you call this tea?

1956
02:02:21,250 --> 02:02:22,500
[knocking on door]

1957
02:02:23,041 --> 02:02:24,166
Who is it?

1958
02:02:24,583 --> 02:02:26,708
[door creaking open]

1959
02:02:45,916 --> 02:02:48,125
Pednekar sir, is everything alright?

1960
02:02:49,458 --> 02:02:51,500
What brings you to this poor man's house
so suddenly?

1961
02:02:51,541 --> 02:02:52,583
You scoundrel...

1962
02:02:53,125 --> 02:02:54,416
Stop your drama.

1963
02:02:55,208 --> 02:02:56,375
The two kids from Kerala?

1964
02:02:56,416 --> 02:02:57,958
These officers have come to take them.

1965
02:02:58,125 --> 02:03:00,291
Look, I have a lot of work. Call them fast.

1966
02:03:00,333 --> 02:03:01,458
What is it, sir?

1967
02:03:01,458 --> 02:03:02,958
Why are you bothering me?

1968
02:03:03,375 --> 02:03:06,041
We don't do anything in your jurisdiction.
So what's the problem?

1969
02:03:06,041 --> 02:03:08,041
Respect the arrangement
we have between us, sir.

1970
02:03:08,083 --> 02:03:09,916
There are no kids from Kerala here.

1971
02:03:10,000 --> 02:03:11,291
Please leave, sir.

1972
02:03:11,291 --> 02:03:13,333
You won't find anything here.
Don't waste your time.

1973
02:03:13,333 --> 02:03:14,333
You scum.

1974
02:03:14,833 --> 02:03:16,291
Madam has information.

1975
02:03:16,708 --> 02:03:18,083
And she has sent them here.

1976
02:03:18,416 --> 02:03:19,541
Shall I leave?

1977
02:03:19,583 --> 02:03:20,750
And tell her the same?

1978
02:03:20,875 --> 02:03:23,208
Let's do one thing, you come with me.
Tell her yourself.

1979
02:03:24,083 --> 02:03:25,458
Hey Gotiya.

1980
02:03:26,458 --> 02:03:27,541
Yes, boss.

1981
02:03:30,541 --> 02:03:31,875
The shelter in Kanthawadi.

1982
02:03:32,291 --> 02:03:33,791
Where the kids are kept.

1983
02:03:33,833 --> 02:03:34,833
Okay.

1984
02:03:35,166 --> 02:03:37,250
Take them there and show them.
Let them be satisfied.

1985
02:03:37,833 --> 02:03:38,958
Go right now.

1986
02:03:39,166 --> 02:03:40,250
Come, sir.

1987
02:03:41,625 --> 02:03:42,708
Come.

1988
02:03:48,291 --> 02:03:50,291
Where is your Jackie Chan?
Haven't seen him lately.

1989
02:03:50,375 --> 02:03:52,166
-You didn't know, sir?
-What?

1990
02:03:52,250 --> 02:03:54,041
Three months ago, Jackie abducted a girl

1991
02:03:54,083 --> 02:03:55,708
from Sawant's territory...

1992
02:03:55,708 --> 02:03:56,625
And then?

1993
02:03:56,625 --> 02:03:57,666
And then what?

1994
02:03:57,666 --> 02:03:59,625
Sawant's men locked Jackie up in Juhu.

1995
02:04:00,208 --> 02:04:02,583
But Jackie beat them the hell out of them.

1996
02:04:02,791 --> 02:04:04,916
Two days later, Jackie went missing.

1997
02:04:05,000 --> 02:04:06,000
What are you saying?

1998
02:04:06,041 --> 02:04:07,291
Yes, sir...

1999
02:04:07,333 --> 02:04:09,500
-Didn't you guys look for him?
-Where to look?

2000
02:04:10,208 --> 02:04:12,041
Sawant must have finished him off.

2001
02:04:12,083 --> 02:04:13,125
And what about the girl?

2002
02:04:13,125 --> 02:04:16,625
China Uncle couriered that girl
along with few other kids.

2003
02:04:16,666 --> 02:04:17,875
Outside Bombay.

2004
02:04:19,041 --> 02:04:20,041
When?

2005
02:04:20,166 --> 02:04:21,958
Sometime around yesterday or day before.

2006
02:04:21,958 --> 02:04:25,291
[melancholic humming]

2007
02:04:35,208 --> 02:04:36,250
Get lost!

2008
02:04:49,500 --> 02:04:51,000
What happened? Where are the kids?

2009
02:04:51,125 --> 02:04:52,666
-They are inside, sir.
-Then what?

2010
02:04:54,583 --> 02:04:56,625
Sir... my hands are pricking...

2011
02:05:03,541 --> 02:05:04,750
Bloody prick!

2012
02:05:05,125 --> 02:05:06,541
This guy has some nerve, huh?

2013
02:05:06,750 --> 02:05:07,833
Keep this.

2014
02:05:08,083 --> 02:05:09,500
Damn, you guys will never change.

2015
02:05:09,625 --> 02:05:10,625
Sir...

2016
02:05:12,208 --> 02:05:13,291
Move now.

2017
02:05:14,291 --> 02:05:15,666
Alright, sir. Come.

2018
02:05:15,791 --> 02:05:17,416
Go inside and see if the kids are there.

2019
02:05:17,458 --> 02:05:18,625
I'll wait right here.

2020
02:05:22,833 --> 02:05:24,750
[children chattering]

2021
02:05:32,666 --> 02:05:34,791
[melancholic humming]

2022
02:05:59,416 --> 02:06:00,541
Hey...

2023
02:06:00,583 --> 02:06:01,833
Get up, kids.

2024
02:06:02,791 --> 02:06:04,375
Everyone get up.

2025
02:06:04,458 --> 02:06:05,750
Get up, get up.

2026
02:06:07,875 --> 02:06:09,625
Get up, you.

2027
02:06:10,291 --> 02:06:12,666
Hey hero, do you need a special invitation?
Get up.

2028
02:06:12,791 --> 02:06:14,208
My leg is injured.

2029
02:06:16,000 --> 02:06:17,333
Take a look, sir.

2030
02:07:34,583 --> 02:07:36,708
<i>Eat a little bit, sweetie.</i>

2031
02:07:36,750 --> 02:07:38,541
<i>You'll be a good girl only if you eat.</i>

2032
02:07:39,208 --> 02:07:41,208
<i>Brother, I don't want.</i>

2033
02:07:45,583 --> 02:07:46,916
<i>Just take one bite.</i>

2034
02:07:47,250 --> 02:07:49,000
<i>I'm not hungry, brother.</i>

2035
02:08:03,708 --> 02:08:04,750
Have it.

2036
02:08:04,791 --> 02:08:06,166
I don't want...

2037
02:08:28,041 --> 02:08:30,208
[melancholic music playing]

2038
02:08:44,625 --> 02:08:46,041
What's your name, dear?

2039
02:08:46,416 --> 02:08:47,833
Meenu.

2040
02:08:50,250 --> 02:08:51,333
Huh?

2041
02:08:51,708 --> 02:08:52,708
Meenu.

2042
02:08:52,750 --> 02:08:56,083
[melancholic music playing]

2043
02:09:00,958 --> 02:09:02,208
Deva.

2044
02:09:23,166 --> 02:09:24,541
Amma...

2045
02:09:27,666 --> 02:09:29,000
Amma...

2046
02:09:31,041 --> 02:09:38,375
<i>♪ If you gently sit upon
the swing of my soul ♪</i>

2047
02:09:38,958 --> 02:09:46,625
<i>♪ I shall swing you ♪</i>

2048
02:09:48,416 --> 02:09:55,666
<i>♪ And in that moment
when boundless grace is showered ♪</i>

2049
02:09:56,708 --> 02:10:04,333
<i>♪ Melting in your love, I too shall sway ♪</i>

2050
02:11:01,791 --> 02:11:07,083
<i>♪ In the darkness,
under the dew-laden moonlight ♪</i>

2051
02:11:07,083 --> 02:11:12,291
<i>♪ Like a tender leaf trembling in the chill ♪</i>

2052
02:11:12,375 --> 02:11:17,750
<i>♪ Why was this blossoming young sprout ♪</i>

2053
02:11:17,791 --> 02:11:22,958
<i>♪ Plucked and cast away by the night? ♪</i>

2054
02:11:23,125 --> 02:11:28,208
<i>♪ Plucked and cast away by the night? ♪</i>

2055
02:11:31,125 --> 02:11:36,250
<i>♪ If you gently sit upon
the swing of my soul ♪</i>

2056
02:11:36,416 --> 02:11:41,833
<i>♪ I shall swing you ♪</i>

2057
02:11:42,666 --> 02:11:45,375
<i>Today is a proud day for Kerala Police.</i>

2058
02:11:45,791 --> 02:11:48,166
<i>All the credit for this goes to Ajeeb.</i>

2059
02:11:48,541 --> 02:11:50,666
<i>This was a case we had all given up on.</i>

2060
02:11:51,125 --> 02:11:53,875
<i>Today, if these children are here with us,</i>

2061
02:11:54,458 --> 02:11:58,625
<i>it is only because of the efforts taken by
Ajeeb and Joy.</i>

2062
02:11:59,333 --> 02:12:03,083
<i>Kerala Police salutes before
their determination.</i>

2063
02:12:03,208 --> 02:12:05,375
[emotional music playing]

2064
02:12:33,666 --> 02:12:35,958
Rescued from Mumbai,
the children are now pursuing

2065
02:12:36,000 --> 02:12:38,041
their education and rebuilding their lives

2066
02:12:38,083 --> 02:12:40,291
under the care of
Mr. Anshad, the investigating officer.

2067
02:12:40,333 --> 02:12:42,083
A golden chapter in Kerala Police history.

2068
02:12:42,083 --> 02:12:43,125
A big salute!

2069
02:13:02,666 --> 02:13:05,333
[emotional music playing]

2070
02:13:07,083 --> 02:13:08,958
Official data from
National Crime Records Bureau

2071
02:13:09,000 --> 02:13:10,625
and Ministry of Women & Child Development

2072
02:13:10,666 --> 02:13:13,083
shows that in 2020,
43,515 children went missing across India.

2073
02:13:13,125 --> 02:13:14,625
Of those, only 38,113 were rescued.

2074
02:13:14,625 --> 02:13:16,916
A chilling reality...
over 5,400 children remain untraced.

2075
02:14:28,375 --> 02:14:33,458
<i>♪ If you gently sit upon
the swing of my soul ♪</i>

2076
02:14:33,541 --> 02:14:38,708
<i>♪ I shall swing you ♪</i>

2077
02:14:39,041 --> 02:14:44,000
<i>♪ And in that moment
when boundless grace is showered ♪</i>

2078
02:14:44,000 --> 02:14:50,208
<i>♪ Melting in your love, I too shall sway ♪</i>

2079
02:15:21,750 --> 02:15:27,041
<i>♪ In the darkness,
under the dew-laden moonlight ♪</i>

2080
02:15:27,041 --> 02:15:32,250
<i>♪ Like a tender leaf trembling in the chill ♪</i>

2081
02:15:32,291 --> 02:15:37,708
<i>♪ Why was this blossoming young sprout ♪</i>

2082
02:15:37,750 --> 02:15:42,916
<i>♪ Plucked and cast away by the night? ♪</i>

2083
02:15:43,083 --> 02:15:48,000
<i>♪ Plucked and cast away by the night? ♪</i>

2084
02:15:51,083 --> 02:15:56,166
<i>♪ If you gently sit upon
the swing of my soul ♪</i>

2085
02:15:56,333 --> 02:16:01,416
<i>♪ I shall swing you ♪</i>

